{id="t0100-01",kind="set",pieces={"CannedCorn","LetterHandwritten"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Food stop on the way out",body="The grocery note says every item was collected before the westbound trip; a food tin remains beside the argument about who should be left in charge.",anchor={map="RiversideStashMap7",mark=1}},
-- T0101
{id="t0101-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Eat before leaving",body="A meal bundle is tied to a note asking the next person to eat before departure; the sighting entry on the reverse is dated after the route was closed.",anchor={map="RiversideStashMap8",mark=1}},
-- T0102
{id="t0102-01",kind="set",pieces={"PetrolCan","Pills"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fuel and a medicine request",body="The fuel can is tagged for a medical pickup; the note says the driver stopped at the marked house after a field worker became ill.",anchor={map="RiversideStashMap9",mark=1}},
-- T0103
{id="t0103-01",kind="set",pieces={"Sponge","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Sponge beside the spare mark",body="the sponge and folded road map are tied with cut warning tape. six tally cuts mark the sponge; only four are crossed through.",anchor={map="RiversideStashMap10",mark=1}},
-- T0104
{id="t0104-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The missing instruction",body="The garden notebook has a removed instruction page and a note asking whether the unopened sample should go with the next supply run.",anchor={map="RosewoodStashMap1",mark=1}},
-- T0105
{id="t0105-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pistol","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The line ends here",body="The route map is folded around a weapon handover slip; the last stop is marked complete, but the return route has no driver.",anchor={map="RosewoodStashMap2",mark=1}},
-- T0106
{id="t0106-01",kind="set",pieces={"Hammer","Nails"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fortify while we wait",body="The repair kit is left with a note to keep the school-side window closed until the ground dries. The family meeting time is written in the same hand.",anchor={map="RosewoodStashMap3",mark=1}},
-- T0107
{id="t0107-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_ALICEpack","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Take what fits",body="The packed bag is tied to a departure card that says to take what fits; the final line sends the group away before the promised pickup.",anchor={map="RosewoodStashMap4",mark=1}},
-- T0109
{id="t0109-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Food for the last visit",body="The meal bag is marked for pickup only after the route opens. Someone has crossed out the driver’s name but left the note to wait for the household.",anchor={map="RosewoodStashMap5",mark=1}},
-- T0110
{id="t0110-01",kind="set",pieces={"ToiletPaper","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="After on the toilet roll, the first copy",body="the toilet roll and water bottle are packed with treated seed. every kernel has the same cracked green coating.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap1",mark=1}},
-- T0111
{id="t0111-01",kind="set",pieces={"Hammer","Nails"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Safe after the barricade",body="A barricade kit is packed beside a key marked for return; the inventory lists the weapons as hidden before the road restriction was posted.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap2",mark=1}},
-- T0112
{id="t0112-01",kind="set",pieces={"PetrolCan","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fuel before the run",body="A fuel can is paired with a route slip for a field visit; the return line says “full” though the can is nearly empty.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap3",mark=1}},
{id="t0112-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wrench stop after the sprayer run",body="Repair note: flush the field sprayer at the wrench mark before returning it. The pump seal had softened and the mechanic wrote that the rinse water stung his hands.\n\nWe kept one copy for ourselves. The person collecting the other one said the numbers would be corrected later, once everyone had moved.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap3",mark=2}},
{id="t0112-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Gas charged to the trial plot",body="Cash receipt: fuel at the marked stop, charged to the late-season crop trial. The driver added that the tank was full before the detour and nearly dry afterward.\n\nThere was a place for a signature and no one willing to write one. I used the margin to note what we actually found.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap3",note=1}},
{id="t0112-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fuel needed for a second pass",body="Notebook line under “you’ll need it”: reserve another can for the second pasture pass. The first crew came home coughing before any emergency convoy used the road.\n\nMy mother put it with the household bills so it would not be thrown away. It was the only part of the week that still had a date.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap3",note=2}},
-- T0113
{id="t0113-01",kind="set",pieces={"Tissue","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Packet of tissues beside the spare mark",body="the packet of tissues and first-aid kit were sealed together but never opened. soot darkens the bundle; clean outlines show it was packed before the fire.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap4",mark=1}},
-- T0114
{id="t0114-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_ALICEpack","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supplies kept out of sight",body="A pack of supplies is hidden with the field bag; a note asks the next visitor to keep the watchers from seeing the unopened test kit.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap5",mark=1}},
-- T0115
{id="t0115-01",kind="set",pieces={"Candle","Clipboard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Candle beside the spare mark",body="matching white stripes cross the candle and clipboard. a name-sized patch on the candle has been scrubbed bare.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap6",mark=1}},
{id="t0115-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cross beside the trial store",body="Photograph back: the cross marks the store used by the crop trial. One sample crate was removed before the inventory and left a blue outline on the floor.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap6",mark=2}},
{id="t0115-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supplies at the first written mark",body="Torn page: there should be sampling jars and boot covers here. The crop crew left them when two workers developed rashes and the planned collection was cancelled.\n\nThe first person who saw it called it routine. The second asked me to stop using the well until another visit could be arranged.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap6",note=1}},
{id="t0115-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Too large for one field crew",body="Personal farm log: “too big to secure” was the old packing floor. The trial team used only one bay, yet fresh powder reached the locked bays overnight.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The notice changed faster than the deliveries, and no one came to collect what was left.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap6",note=2}},
{id="t0115-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cross checked after the seed delivery",body="Receipt margin: count the sealed seed sacks again at the cross. The driver signed for twelve, while only eleven appear on the field tally.\n\nNobody agreed on whose list this belonged to. I left it where the next person would look for the things we still owed each other.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap6",note=3}},
{id="t0115-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Initials beside the plot count",body="On a faded photograph: the handwritten name by the cross belonged to the man counting treated rows. His tally ends one row before the plants turned black.\n\nI meant to ask about it in the morning. By then the person who could answer had gone with the last vehicle, and this was all that remained.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap6",note=4}},
-- T0116
{id="t0116-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bandage","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fill before the building empties",body="The water bottle is tagged for the infected area, but the field note says to fill it before the next crew enters. A bandage wrapper is folded around the cap.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap7",mark=1}},
-- T0117
{id="t0117-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A destination without a name",body="The route page is complete except for its destination. The departure box is checked, and a margin asks the driver to wait for an updated order.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap8",mark=1}},
-- T0118
{id="t0118-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Crates without contents",body="A crate tally includes the offices but lists no contents; the next page labels the same shipment for a field check.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",mark=1}},
{id="t0118-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Crates reserved for field samples",body="Warehouse note: keep the empty crates for soil cores from the southern trial farms. Three returned damp and smelling of solvent, though the manifest lists them unused.\n\nSomeone said the smell was only from cleaning. I kept the scrap because the same smell had followed us from the previous stop.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=1}},
{id="t0118-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Railyard pickup before dawn",body="Diary entry: the railyard pickup carried seed sacks and rinse drums before dawn. By breakfast the switchman’s eyes burned; the public closure came later.\n\nThe mark was made in a hurry, before the queue moved. I checked it twice against the people standing with me.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=2}},
{id="t0118-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Muldraugh route crossed out",body="Driver’s torn page: the Muldraugh route was crossed out after the field team reported foam in the drainage ditch. No replacement destination appears.\n\nOur copy stayed on the kitchen table. The official account came later and asked us to remember a much shorter day.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=3}},
{id="t0118-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Muldraugh field route in the margin",body="Driver’s diary: beside the Muldraugh label, the return route from the southern trial farms is written in pencil. Two stops are rubbed out, but their sample counts remain.\n\nI took the page when they shut the building. No one could tell me whether the missing line meant delayed, refused, or already gone.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=4}},
{id="t0118-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Office ledger with no owner",body="Notebook from the offices: four crop-test invoices, no company name, all paid in cash. A pencil note says the county men collected the carbon copies.\n\nA pencil line had been rubbed thin but not erased. I could still read enough of it to recognize what had been there first.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=5}},
{id="t0118-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Warehouse bay washed twice",body="Cleaning receipt: warehouse bay three was washed twice after storing pasture-treatment drums. The second wash is billed before the first crew signed out.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=6}},
{id="t0118-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Trains idle after the shipment",body="Personal rail log: none of the trains would start after the trial shipment arrived. The same oily grit coated each air intake, but the repair report calls it ordinary dust.\n\nThe children asked why the same place had two different names on the two papers. I told them to hold on to both until we knew.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap9",note=7}},
-- T0119
{id="t0119-01",kind="set",pieces={"Matches","HandTorch"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Box of matches beside the spare mark",body="the box of matches and hand torch smell sharply of bleach. mud outlines between them show that a third object was removed.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",mark=1}},
{id="t0119-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Clothes bag from the test rows",body="Laundry receipt: coveralls from the second circle carried orange pollen from the test rows. The clerk noted numb fingers before patrol cars reached the highway.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. When I asked, the person at the barrier looked at the seal instead and handed it back.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",mark=2}},
{id="t0119-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Lunch stop for the field crew",body="Meal receipt back: six lunches went to the greenhouse crew at the third circle. Two were untouched; beside them someone wrote, “metal taste after noon spray.”\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",mark=3}},
{id="t0119-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cars rinsed behind the garage",body="Photograph note: the fourth circle shows where three field cars were hosed down. Pale foam ran toward the ditch while the garage was still open to families.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",mark=4}},
{id="t0119-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fuel for the orchard rig",body="Pocket ledger: gas at this circle was charged to the orchard rig, not the relief trucks. The return mileage exceeds the marked field route by forty miles.\n\nThe first person who saw it called it routine. The second asked me to stop using the well until another visit could be arranged.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",note=1}},
{id="t0119-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Coveralls kept off the invoice",body="Torn note under the clothes label: bag the trial coveralls separately and leave them off the laundry invoice. My wrists blistered while tying the second bag.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The notice changed faster than the deliveries, and no one came to collect what was left.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",note=2}},
{id="t0119-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field lunches at the restaurant",body="Receipt from the marked restaurant: lunches for the crop crew, plus soap and bottled water. A handwritten line says the tap smelled sharp before closing.\n\nNobody agreed on whose list this belonged to. I left it where the next person would look for the things we still owed each other.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",note=3}},
{id="t0119-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fleet note with one car missing",body="Farm-program mileage page: four cars left for the plots, three returned for washing. The blank driver line is dated before the county barricade went up.\n\nI meant to ask about it in the morning. By then the person who could answer had gone with the last vehicle, and this was all that remained.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",note=4}},
{id="t0119-09",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Car label beside a field rinse bill",body="Garage receipt at the car label: rinse three crop-study vehicles and keep the fourth outside. The fourth plate is the only one copied into the county log.\n\nThe small ordinary expense was the part I could still account for. I could not make the other figure on this page match what I had seen.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",note=5}},
{id="t0119-10",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Final circle after the convoy left",body="Notebook line at the final circle: one trial car returned after the others had gone. Its seats were dusted white and its mileage page had been removed.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. Someone wanted the book put away before I had even finished copying it.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap10",note=6}},
-- T0120
{id="t0120-01",kind="set",pieces={"RadioReceiver","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A signal sent for testing",body="The radio test sheet says the signal dropped at the tower; the technician’s note asks the field crew to check power before changing equipment.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap11",mark=1}},
{id="t0120-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Dish three carried plot readings",body="Personal service note: dish three on tower two relayed moisture readings from the trial plots. The signal vanished during the night application, before any public emergency traffic.\n\nThe small ordinary expense was the part I could still account for. I could not make the other figure on this page match what I had seen.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap11",note=1}},
{id="t0120-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Power dip during the field pass",body="Torn meter log: near six gigahertz, power dipped as the spraying crew entered the eastern field. The station batteries were full and no storm was recorded.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. Someone wanted the book put away before I had even finished copying it.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap11",note=2}},
{id="t0120-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Test request with samples attached",body="Letter draft: ask headquarters to compare the Lexington receiver with two leaf samples. The samples carry the same gray film found inside the tower cabinet.\n\nThe person who handed this to me asked me to keep the date. I did, though the next version left that day out entirely.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap11",note=3}},
{id="t0120-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sun mark over the crop receiver",body="Photograph back at the sun mark: the crop-weather receiver is lit, but its plot channel reads blank. The operator noted a chemical smell inside the cabinet.\n\nI carried it home because there was nowhere open to return it. The mark did not come off when I tried to wash my hands.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap11",note=4}},
{id="t0120-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cross placed over the test receiver",body="Technician’s notebook: the cross marks the receiver used for crop-weather telemetry. It failed whenever the treated field pump ran, then recovered after the pump stopped.\n\nWe kept one copy for ourselves. The person collecting the other one said the numbers would be corrected later, once everyone had moved.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap11",note=5}},
-- T0121
{id="t0121-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pills","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Camp supplies minus one person",body="The camp list counts water and medicine but leaves one person’s pickup line blank. A note asks whether the missing dose is still at the main office.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap12",mark=1}},
-- T0122
{id="t0122-01",kind="set",pieces={"LetterHandwritten","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="You have to leave",body="A seed bag is wrapped in a letter asking someone to leave before the field crew returns. The writer says the route is safer if no one waits at the door.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap13",mark=1}},
-- T0123
{id="t0123-01",kind="set",pieces={"Lighter","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Lighter beside the spare mark",body="red and blue cord join the lighter to the bath towel. the red route is cut; the blue route ends in a sealed knot.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap14",mark=1}},
-- T0124
{id="t0124-01",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The garden page",body="A water bottle rests on a garden record whose test result is missing. The last instruction says not to water until the next visit.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap15",mark=1}},
-- T0125
{id="t0125-01",kind="set",pieces={"Extinguisher","Camera"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Fire extinguisher beside the spare mark",body="chalk numbers run across the fire extinguisher and camera. the count skips one place, then resumes in a different hand.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",mark=1}},
{id="t0125-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First trap held a torn field tag",body="Diary line at the first trap: a torn pasture-test tag was caught beneath the spring. Its number belongs to a drum the return ledger calls sealed.\n\nThere was a place for a signature and no one willing to write one. I used the margin to note what we actually found.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=1}},
{id="t0125-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Camp used by the pasture team",body="Camp log: the pasture-study team slept here for three nights. On the fourth morning their cook poured out the water because it smelled medicinal.\n\nMy mother put it with the household bills so it would not be thrown away. It was the only part of the week that still had a date.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=2}},
{id="t0125-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="North arrow past the wash drums",body="Field diary: the first north arrow leads past drums used to wash pasture-test gear. One drum was already sealed when the checkpoint crew arrived.\n\nThe first account was spoken quickly, as if there might be a bus to catch. I wrote it down before another person could replace it.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=3}},
{id="t0125-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second trap held a sample bag",body="Photograph back: the second trap contained a torn soil-sample bag, not an animal. Blue granules beneath it matched the coating on the trial seed.\n\nI asked for the old page back after the new instructions arrived. They said it had been destroyed, but its corner was still in my pocket.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=4}},
{id="t0125-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Checkpoint checked field badges",body="Personal note from the checkpoint: wave through the green field badges before recording civilian plates. I copied one badge number after its wearer began shaking.\n\nThe person beside me recognized the handwriting and went quiet. We had been told not to rely on yesterday’s directions.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=5}},
{id="t0125-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Barriers moved after the spill",body="Road-crew receipt: barriers were moved downhill after a trial drum leaked. The billed time is two hours before the radio announced an emergency route.\n\nI set it aside to show the neighbor when she returned. Her porch was empty by the time the light was good enough to read it.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=6}},
{id="t0125-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Upper arrow toward the trial gate",body="Torn page: follow the upper north arrow to the trial gate and count every rinse can. The crew counted seven going in and six coming back.\n\nThey counted the containers before anyone counted who had carried them. I wrote the second number here while I could still remember it.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap16",note=7}},
-- T0126
{id="t0126-01",kind="set",pieces={"Camera","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photographs from the blind spot",body="A camera is packed with a field notebook that says to photograph the blind side of the fence; the sensor check is marked complete before the crew arrives.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap17",mark=1}},
-- T0127
{id="t0127-01",kind="set",pieces={"AlcoholWipes","Briefcase"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Alcohol wipes beside the spare mark",body="the alcohol wipes and briefcase are wrapped in a child's raincoat. one stayed dry while the other was left in road mud.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",mark=1}},
{id="t0127-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First fire under the assay table",body="Farm diary: the first fire started beneath the assay table after a field sample cracked. The wet soil burned blue before any building caught.\n\nI took the page when they shut the building. No one could tell me whether the missing line meant delayed, refused, or already gone.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=1}},
{id="t0127-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second fire, scorched assay tray",body="Diary entry: beside the second fire mark lay a scorched tray from the soil assay. Its unburned label says the orchard batch was reapplied after rain.\n\nA pencil line had been rubbed thin but not erased. I could still read enough of it to recognize what had been there first.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=2}},
{id="t0127-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Third fire, seed sacks first",body="Photograph back: the third fire began among returned seed sacks, not the nearby lumber. Violet grains remained in the seams after the flames went out.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=3}},
{id="t0127-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fourth fire beside the rinse pit",body="Farm log: smoke at the fourth fire rose from the rinse pit after the trial crew emptied its hoses. The grass died in a clean ring before dusk.\n\nThe children asked why the same place had two different names on the two papers. I told them to hold on to both until we knew.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=4}},
{id="t0127-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fifth fire after the drum split",body="Torn notebook page: the fifth fire followed a split treatment drum. Water spread the burning film, so we covered it with field soil and left.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. When I asked, the person at the barrier looked at the seal instead and handed it back.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=5}},
{id="t0127-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sixth fire on the sample route",body="Receipt margin: replace two boots burned at the sixth fire on the sampling route. Both soles carried the same sticky amber residue.\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=6}},
{id="t0127-08",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seventh fire at the hay edge",body="Letter draft: the seventh fire caught damp hay where the pasture spray settled. The extension worker asked us to call it a lantern accident.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=7}},
{id="t0127-09",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Eighth fire before sunrise",body="Diary line: the eighth fire glowed before sunrise around bags from the night application. No homes were burning and no siren had sounded.\n\nThe first person who saw it called it routine. The second asked me to stop using the well until another visit could be arranged.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=8}},
{id="t0127-10",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Ninth fire by the drainage cut",body="Photograph note: the ninth fire follows the drainage cut from the experimental plot. Frogs floated below it while the bank still smoked.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The notice changed faster than the deliveries, and no one came to collect what was left.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=9}},
{id="t0127-11",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tenth fire under the sprayer",body="Maintenance page: the tenth fire blackened the parked sprayer from beneath. The fuel line was intact; dried treatment foam covered the hot shield.\n\nNobody agreed on whose list this belonged to. I left it where the next person would look for the things we still owed each other.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=10}},
{id="t0127-12",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Eleventh fire and empty cages",body="Personal note: after the eleventh fire, every test cage stood open. The rabbits were gone, but their water pans held white crystals.\n\nI meant to ask about it in the morning. By then the person who could answer had gone with the last vehicle, and this was all that remained.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=11}},
{id="t0127-13",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Twelfth fire at the row flags",body="Farm diary: the twelfth fire consumed only the flagged crop rows. Untreated rows on either side stayed green until the next rain.\n\nThe small ordinary expense was the part I could still account for. I could not make the other figure on this page match what I had seen.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=12}},
{id="t0127-14",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Thirteenth fire behind the shed",body="Feed receipt back: at the thirteenth fire we found six empty additive tins behind the shed. The purchase line lists five.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. Someone wanted the book put away before I had even finished copying it.\n\nThe next morning I looked for a second copy and found only the envelope. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=13}},
{id="t0127-15",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fourteenth fire along wet ground",body="Notebook sketch: the fourteenth fire crawled across wet ground in the same path as yesterday’s trial runoff. Ordinary straw would not burn there.\n\nThe person who handed this to me asked me to keep the date. I did, though the next version left that day out entirely.\n\nThe next morning I looked for a second copy and found only the envelope. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=14}},
{id="t0127-16",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fifteenth fire and the buried jar",body="Letter fragment: beneath the fifteenth fire mark I buried a sealed leaf jar. Its leaves spotted black before the heat reached them.\n\nI carried it home because there was nowhere open to return it. The mark did not come off when I tried to wash my hands.\n\nThe next morning I looked for a second copy and found only the envelope. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=15}},
{id="t0127-17",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sad face after the field meal",body="Diary line at the sad face: the field cook wept when three workers could not swallow lunch. All had handled the new grain coating that morning.\n\nWe kept one copy for ourselves. The person collecting the other one said the numbers would be corrected later, once everyone had moved.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=16}},
{id="t0127-18",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Gun beside the locked sample case",body="Photograph back at the first gun: a guard watched the sample case while the sick applicator waited outside. The case left before the ambulance came.\n\nI wrote this on the back because nobody would take a statement. The guard never looked at the man on the step, only at the case, as if the case was the patient.\n\nWhen the van came for it the driver signed nothing. I kept the picture in my coat until my hands stopped shaking, then put it away where I keep the bills.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=17}},
{id="t0127-19",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Happy face on the bonus sheet",body="Pay-envelope note at the first happy face: bonus for completing the late spray despite complaints. My hands were numb when I signed.\n\nThe foreman drew the smiling face himself, said it meant we had earned it. Two of the crew had already gone home coughing and still got the same envelope, sealed, no questions.\n\nI have not spent it. It is folded inside this note, and I keep telling myself the numbness is only from the cold mornings.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=18}},
{id="t0127-20",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First dead face, stained gloves",body="Torn diary page: at the first dead face, stained gloves remained beside a crop-trial badge. The public list later called the wearer an unknown traveler.\n\nI knew him. He ate at our table twice and talked about the test rows like they were his children. Nobody who knew his name was asked.\n\nI tore this page out so it would not sit in the diary with the ordinary days. If someone finds it, the badge number is on the back.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=19}},
{id="t0127-21",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second dead face by the well",body="Notebook line: the second dead face marks the well tender who sampled cloudy water for the pasture study. His bottle disappeared before dawn.\n\nHe told me the water smelled sweet, like the drums behind the equipment shed. He meant to drive the bottle to town himself because the study people never came back for the last ones.\n\nThe truck was still in his yard. The bottle was not. I copied his sample dates from the pump house wall before they painted it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=20}},
{id="t0127-22",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Third dead face near clean corn",body="Photograph note: the third dead face lies beside corn that looks untouched. A trial flag was pulled from the row but its wire hole remains.\n\nThe person beside me recognized the handwriting and went quiet. We had been told not to rely on yesterday’s directions.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=21}},
{id="t0127-23",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fourth dead face on the truck path",body="Mileage slip back: the fourth dead face was found on the field truck path. Tire tracks lead away before the road closure begins.\n\nI set it aside to show the neighbor when she returned. Her porch was empty by the time the light was good enough to read it.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=22}},
{id="t0127-24",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fifth dead face and the wash basin",body="Diary entry: the fifth dead face is beside the crew wash basin. The water smelled of bleach and the rinse ledger had been torn out.\n\nThey counted the containers before anyone counted who had carried them. I wrote the second number here while I could still remember it.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=23}},
{id="t0127-25",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sixth dead face under orchard netting",body="Torn letter: at the sixth dead face, orchard netting covered a man still wearing sample tags. The fruit above him had split without ripening.\n\nThe clerk wanted a cleaner version. I kept the stained one because it showed which part had been changed after the road closed.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=24}},
{id="t0127-26",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seventh dead face at the feed cart",body="Receipt note: the seventh dead face fell beside feed mixed for the supplement trial. The cart number is absent from the barn account.\n\nI did not know where to put it after the shelves were cleared. There was still someone coming back for the answer written on it.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=25}},
{id="t0127-27",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Eighth dead face beyond the flags",body="Personal map note: the eighth dead face lay beyond the last trial flag, where the wind carried the mist. Officials later measured only inside the flags.\n\nWe waited for a correction that never came. Every passing driver had a different instruction and no room for one more passenger.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=26}},
{id="t0127-28",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Ninth dead face and the sealed flask",body="Notebook page: a sealed flask beside the ninth dead face contains green field water. The label asks for testing, but no laboratory is named.\n\nI had promised to bring this home for supper. Its date and the empty chair at the table now belong to the same evening.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=27}},
{id="t0127-29",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second happy face on a clean report",body="Photograph back at the second happy face: the supervisor held up a clean inspection sheet while smoke rose behind the trial rows.\n\nSomeone said the smell was only from cleaning. I kept the scrap because the same smell had followed us from the previous stop.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=28}},
{id="t0127-30",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second gun guarding rinse records",body="Diary margin at the second gun: an armed man collected the rinse records and left the seed invoices. He wore no county badge.\n\nThe mark was made in a hurry, before the queue moved. I checked it twice against the people standing with me.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=29}},
{id="t0127-31",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second sad face beside calf tags",body="Letter fragment at the second sad face: twelve calf tags came back from the supplement pasture, but only eleven calves were unloaded.\n\nOur copy stayed on the kitchen table. The official account came later and asked us to remember a much shorter day.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=30}},
{id="t0127-32",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First skull, rejected soil core",body="Field log at the first skull: this soil core was rejected for a sharp solvent smell. The replacement core came from outside the treated rows.\n\nI took the page when they shut the building. No one could tell me whether the missing line meant delayed, refused, or already gone.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=31}},
{id="t0127-33",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Second skull, rain-barrel sample",body="Receipt back at the second skull: one rain-barrel sample, paid cash. The barrel stood downwind of the experimental orchard.\n\nA pencil line had been rubbed thin but not erased. I could still read enough of it to recognize what had been there first.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=32}},
{id="t0127-34",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Third skull, birds under the wire",body="Diary line at the third skull: birds dropped beneath the plot wire after dawn spraying. The crew buried them before opening the gate.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=33}},
{id="t0127-35",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fourth skull, missing drum weight",body="Warehouse note at the fourth skull: the returned treatment drum weighed nine pounds less than dispatch. Its seal appeared untouched.\n\nThe children asked why the same place had two different names on the two papers. I told them to hold on to both until we knew.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=34}},
{id="t0127-36",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fifth skull, milk poured away",body="Farm notebook at the fifth skull: pour away milk from the test pasture until told otherwise. The instruction arrived before the cattle looked ill.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. When I asked, the person at the barrier looked at the seal instead and handed it back.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=35}},
{id="t0127-37",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sixth skull, blackened bean leaves",body="Photograph back at the sixth skull: bean leaves blackened in the shape of yesterday’s spray fan. The roots remained pale and firm.\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=36}},
{id="t0127-38",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seventh skull, final field count",body="Torn ledger at the seventh skull: the final field count omits two applicators and one sample case. Their truck is still marked returned.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap18",note=37}},
-- T0128
{id="t0128-01",kind="set",pieces={"Pistol","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Weapons beside the supply sack",body="A seed bag and weapon are listed on the same storage slip; the note asks the visitor to take only what can be carried after the work is done.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap19",mark=1}},
-- T0129
{id="t0129-01",kind="set",pieces={"SheetPaper2","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Names replaced by insults",body="The access complaint has no names or dates, only a list of doors refused and a final mark that says the crew left.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap20",mark=1}},
-- T0130
{id="t0130-01",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Plot with no note",body="The seed bag is kept beside a water bottle; the notebook page where the plot directions should be has been removed.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap21",mark=1}},
{id="t0130-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Apple mark beside treated windfalls",body="Orchard diary: at the apple mark, windfalls carried a waxy film after the trial pass. The buyer rejected them before any evacuation notice.\n\nI set it aside to show the neighbor when she returned. Her porch was empty by the time the light was good enough to read it.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap21",mark=2}},
{id="t0130-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hammer mark for a sealed pump",body="Repair receipt: the hammer mark identifies the pump sealed after drawing cloudy field water. Its gasket was new, yet the metal inside had turned green.\n\nThey counted the containers before anyone counted who had carried them. I wrote the second number here while I could still remember it.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap21",mark=3}},
{id="t0130-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fuel symbol on the sprayer account",body="Cash slip at the fuel symbol: twelve gallons for the trial sprayer, though its tank holds eight. The clerk wrote the excess under a second farm number.\n\nThe clerk wanted a cleaner version. I kept the stained one because it showed which part had been changed after the road closed.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap21",note=1}},
{id="t0130-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Apple symbol and the rejected crate",body="Photograph back at the apple symbol: the rejected fruit crate has clean skins on top and spotted fruit underneath. A field-trial ribbon is tied to one handle.\n\nI did not know where to put it after the shelves were cleared. There was still someone coming back for the answer written on it.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap21",note=2}},
{id="t0130-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hammer symbol over a green gasket",body="Repair note at the hammer symbol: replace the pump gasket after the experimental feed runoff. The old rubber had turned green without cracking.\n\nWe waited for a correction that never came. Every passing driver had a different instruction and no room for one more passenger.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap21",note=3}},
-- T0131
{id="t0131-01",kind="set",pieces={"Hammer","Nails"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Base camp repairs",body="A repair kit is set beside a base plan; the entry marked secure is dated before the door brace was installed.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap22",mark=1}},
-- T0132
{id="t0132-01",kind="set",pieces={"PetrolCan","Notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Basement supply record",body="The fuel can is tagged for basement storage and the notebook records a test visit on the same date. The return box for the container is empty.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap23",mark=1}},
{id="t0132-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hammer beside the basement vent",body="Maintenance note: use the hammer mark to find the basement vent. Yellow dust appeared inside after the seed-treatment truck idled above it.\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap23",mark=2}},
{id="t0132-03",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fuel mark on the crop account",body="Cash receipt at the fuel mark: the crop-study truck took two cans but returned one. The driver wrote that the missing can stayed with the basement samples.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap23",note=1}},
{id="t0132-04",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Thunder Gas charged the field account",body="Fuel receipt headed “Thunder Gas”: two cans billed to the county crop trial. One can returned with a sharp herbal smell and no cap.\n\nThe first person who saw it called it routine. The second asked me to stop using the well until another visit could be arranged.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap23",note=2}},
{id="t0132-05",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hammer mark over a sealed vent",body="Photograph back at the hammer mark: the basement vent was nailed shut after yellow dust appeared inside. The treatment truck had idled directly above it.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The notice changed faster than the deliveries, and no one came to collect what was left.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap23",note=3}},
{id="t0132-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Basement shelf of leaf samples",body="Diary line under “basement”: leaf jars from three farms occupied the lower shelf. By morning every label had been peeled away, but the dates remained on the lids.\n\nNobody agreed on whose list this belonged to. I left it where the next person would look for the things we still owed each other.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={map="WorldStashMap23",note=4}},
