-- T0282
{id="t0282-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Friday’s entertainment",body="The bar’s entertainment list is clipped to a water check for the back room; the beverage delivery was marked complete before the door was opened.",anchor={print="Twiggys"}},
-- T0283
{id="t0283-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="After sack by the counter, the first copy",body="The pair is streaked with marked feed sack from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the counter unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBBar"}},
{id="t0283-02",kind="set",pieces={"GlassTumbler","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The glass nobody collected",body="The glass was rinsed but the strip of tape stays on it, marked to be kept after closing. The cloth is stiff with bleach. Someone expected the counter to be cleaned before the glass was taken away.",anchor={scene="RBBar"}},
-- T0284
{id="t0284-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="At dusk: rinsed gloves",body="My note from at dusk: the field trial crew carried rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that the siren began.\n\nThe first account was spoken quickly, as if there might be a bus to catch. I wrote it down before another person could replace it.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RBBarn"}},
{id="t0284-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Count the calves as absent",body="I told them the barn was empty after the morning count. It was true if you counted people. The two calves were still there, and I could hear the smaller one pressing its head against the gate whenever a truck stopped outside.\n\nA man I had never seen asked for the ledger, then asked whether I kept another. I said the kitchen calendar had the births on it. He took that too. By evening the gate had a new chain. Nobody asked me to feed them, and nobody said I could go back in.\n\nI left the milk pail by the door because I thought a person who came to lock it would see it. In the morning the pail was gone. The chain was still there.",anchor={scene="RBBarn"}},
-- T0285
{id="t0285-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar with its clouded rim",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the cab unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBBurnt"}},
{id="t0285-02",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A waterline after the fire",body="The kit is unopened. The water bottle has a black line drawn halfway down it and the same line repeated on the charred wall. Whoever marked it was measuring what survived the fire, not treating a burn.",anchor={scene="RBBurnt"}},
-- T0286
{id="t0286-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Near midnight: sealed seed packet",body="I kept the sealed seed packet you asked about. The trial crew passed near midnight; my brother started coughing, and only later a patrol turned everyone back.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={scene="RBBurntCorpse"}},
{id="t0286-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="For the dog, if anyone asks",body="If they ask you who started it, tell them I went inside for the dog. I did. I also went back for the little box under the sink, the one with the dates written on the lid.\n\nThe men outside told me to leave it where it was. One held the door while the other watched me search. When I came out without it, they let me sit by the truck. They were careful with me then. They had already put the box in a bag of their own.\n\nThe dog came out through the back, singed and furious. Please give her water first. I don't want her remembered as another thing I left inside.",anchor={scene="RBBurntCorpse"}},
-- T0287
{id="t0287-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="After sack by the kitchen chair, the first copy",body="The two items are bundled beside marked feed sack; field dust lies beneath them, while a strip of road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBBurntFireman"}},
{id="t0287-02",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Ash inside the sealed jar",body="The jar contains ash beneath its lid. A potato is wrapped in a clean bandage beside it. These were packed together before the fire spread; the jar was being carried out, while the food was left where it could be found.",anchor={scene="RBBurntFireman"}},
-- T0288
{id="t0288-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before breakfast: rinsed gloves",body="before breakfast: the crop trial crew brought rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice before the buses quit running.\n\nThere was a place for a signature and no one willing to write one. I used the margin to note what we actually found.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={scene="RBCafe"}},
{id="t0288-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Names with breakfast",body="The woman at the next table asked why they were taking names with the breakfast order. I told her it was probably for the bill. The waitress folded the list and put it in her apron, though we had all paid at the counter.\n\nLater a man came in through the kitchen, spoke to her, and left with the folded paper. Nobody cleared our plates while he was there. I kept looking at the clock because my sister was due to meet me.\n\nShe never arrived. I wrote down the time, then crossed it out when I realized I couldn't remember whether the clock had stopped before or after the man came in. The waitress set a fresh pot on the stove and kept serving everyone else.",anchor={scene="RBCafe"}},
-- T0289
{id="t0289-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar with its clouded rim",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the coat pocket unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBClinic"}},
{id="t0289-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A dial that cannot turn",body="The battery is taped into the radio with a strip cut from a medicine label. The dial is fixed in place. The clinic kept a receiver ready on one frequency even after ordinary broadcasts had stopped.",anchor={scene="RBClinic"}},
-- T0290
{id="t0290-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before dawn: sealed seed packet",body="My note from before dawn: the field trial crew carried sealed seed packet. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that the county van arrived.\n\nI took the page when they shut the building. No one could tell me whether the missing line meant delayed, refused, or already gone.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={scene="RBDorm"}},
{id="t0290-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Eight names on six beds",body="Room count at noon: four beds slept in, six beds assigned, eight names on the door. Nobody could explain the difference. We had made the list from the doors because the office list had been taken.\n\nA visitor came back with the office list in her hand and asked us to erase two names. She did not ask whether either student was still here. We argued about it quietly because the girl in the end bed was asleep.\n\nBy supper the visitor had gone. I wrote the two names again on a scrap and pushed it into my shoe. If somebody asks tomorrow, I can say I made a mistake. I would rather have a mistake I can show them.",anchor={scene="RBDorm"}},
-- T0291
{id="t0291-01",kind="set",pieces={"FishingRod","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="After sack by the toolbox, the first copy",body="The pair is streaked with marked feed sack from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the toolbox unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBGunstoreSiege"}},
{id="t0291-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The spare receiver",body="A battery sits beside a radio whose tuning knob has been removed. The barricade can hear a single station, but no one inside can change it.",anchor={scene="RBGunstoreSiege"}},
-- T0292
{id="t0292-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tuesday, after opening",body="Three customers from the east fields brought the same sweet chemical smell in their hair. They said the crop trial crew had sprayed before sunrise. I washed everyone twice; by noon a county van had blocked the road.\n\nI carried it home because there was nowhere open to return it. The mark did not come off when I tried to wash my hands.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={scene="RBHairSalon"}},
{id="t0292-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Appointments crossed out",body="I kept the book open so they could see when the last customer had come in. The woman asked for the names instead of the times.\n\nShe did not take the whole book. She tore out two pages and left the small notes about hair color and the money owed. One customer had asked me to call his wife. I still have her number, but I cannot remember which page it was on.\n\nWe swept after they left. A curl of paper caught under the chair and I put it here in case the customer comes back to pay.",anchor={scene="RBHairSalon"}},
-- T0293
{id="t0293-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar with its clouded rim",body="The two items are bundled beside clouded sample jar; field dust lies beneath them, while a strip of road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBHeatBreakAfternoon"}},
{id="t0293-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A sealed morning route",body="The map is folded to hide three streets, and the water bottle has a fresh mark for each one. Whoever drove here was counting stops before anyone on the road knew there was a route.",anchor={scene="RBHeatBreakAfternoon"}},
-- T0294
{id="t0294-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="At dusk: sealed seed packet",body="at dusk: the crop trial crew brought sealed seed packet. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice before the siren began.\n\nThe mark was made in a hurry, before the queue moved. I checked it twice against the people standing with me.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={scene="RBJoanHartford"}},
{id="t0294-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The visitor list",body="They told us the list was for families. I believed them until the families arrived and nobody would let them see it.\n\nOne woman recognized a coat through the window. The man at the door said the coat belonged to a different person and closed the curtain. She waited for hours because no one would tell her whose coat she had seen.\n\nI wrote down the time they took the list. If she comes back I can at least tell her when we stopped being allowed to answer.",anchor={scene="RBJoanHartford"}},
-- T0295
{id="t0295-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="After sack by the cab, the first copy",body="The pair is streaked with marked feed sack from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the cab unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBJudge"}},
{id="t0295-02",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The second date",body="The notebook has two dates written over one another. A pencil laid across it points to the earlier entry, where the margin says that the hearing was closed before anyone arrived.",anchor={scene="RBJudge"}},
-- T0296
{id="t0296-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Near midnight: rinsed gloves",body="My note from near midnight: the field trial crew carried rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that a patrol turned everyone back.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. Someone wanted the book put away before I had even finished copying it.\n\nThe next morning I looked for a second copy and found only the envelope. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={scene="RBLooted"}},
{id="t0296-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Things left behind the lock",body="They came while the room was still full. I thought they were stopping the stealing, but one of them knew which drawer held the names.\n\nI stood outside with a neighbor who was holding a lamp. We heard drawers open, then the men carried out one thin folder. They left the money and the jewelry where the thieves had scattered it.\n\nIn the morning the front door was broken and everyone said the folder had been stolen with the rest. I could not persuade the neighbor to say what we had seen.",anchor={scene="RBLooted"}},
-- T0297
{id="t0297-01",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar with its clouded rim",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the kitchen chair unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBMayorWestPoint"}},
{id="t0297-02",kind="set",pieces={"Newspaper","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two versions of the notice",body="A public notice and a pencil stub are folded together. The penciled time is earlier than the printed one, and someone has marked the first version to be collected before the doors opened.",anchor={scene="RBMayorWestPoint"}},
-- T0298
{id="t0298-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before breakfast: sealed seed packet",body="I kept the sealed seed packet you asked about. The trial crew passed before breakfast; my brother started coughing, and only later the buses quit running.\n\nI had promised to bring this home for supper. Its date and the empty chair at the table now belong to the same evening.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={scene="RBNolans"}},
{id="t0298-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A knock after dark",body="The first man said they were checking on us. The second asked which neighbors had left and wrote their names before he asked whether they were well.\n\nI told them the little boy next door was with his aunt. He had gone to fetch her because she was alone. When the men returned, they asked me to say that both houses had been empty since noon.\n\nI can say I misunderstood the hour. I cannot explain why they came back to change it.",anchor={scene="RBNolans"}},
-- T0299
{id="t0299-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed sack beneath the coat hem",body="The two items are bundled beside marked feed sack; field dust lies beneath them, while a strip of road tape is caught around the bundle.",anchor={scene="RBOffice"}},
{id="t0299-02",kind="set",pieces={"Sheet","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Carbon under the blotter",body="A sheet of paper has been pressed over a handwritten count. The marks beneath still show a larger number than the typed line above it. Someone saved the carbon but discarded the original.",anchor={scene="RBOffice"}},
-- T0300
{id="t0300-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Before dawn: rinsed gloves",body="before dawn: the crop trial crew brought rinsed gloves. my brother started coughing. I washed everything twice before the county van arrived.\n\nI meant to ask about it in the morning. By then the person who could answer had gone with the last vehicle, and this was all that remained.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={scene="RBOther"}},
{id="t0300-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="What the messenger carried",body="He wanted the room cleared before he opened his bag. We moved the chairs into the hall and he put three envelopes on the table.\n\nThe first was for the people still here. The other two had names of places already shut. He took those away when I asked him why he had come so late.\n\nI thought he would leave a copy. Instead he asked for the empty envelopes back, too. The chairs are still in the hall because no one knows whether the room is open.",anchor={scene="RBOther"}},
-- T0301
{id="t0301-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The sample lid turned opaque",body="The pair is streaked with clouded sample jar from treated rows. It was set aside after the flies vanished, before anyone marked the toolbox unsafe.",anchor={scene="RBPileOCrepe"}},
{id="t0301-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The flour stayed behind",body="I was told to leave the kitchen open for one more shift, though the road count already included its address. I set aside a clean apron for the morning cook. The second list, the one for people waiting inside, came back with no names.",anchor={scene="RBPileOCrepe"}},
-- T0302
{id="t0302-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Near lunchtime: sealed seed packet",body="My note from near lunchtime: the field trial crew carried sealed seed packet. my brother started coughing. I had not yet heard that the bridge was blocked.\n\nI did not know where to put it after the shelves were cleared. There was still someone coming back for the answer written on it.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={scene="RBPizzaWhirled"}},
{id="t0302-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Back door count",body="At closing I counted the remaining boxes and wrote the number on the lid. A driver came for them after I had put away the register.\n\nHe had a list of addresses, but it was folded so I could only see the first. He crossed it out without unloading anything. We waited until his radio called him away.\n\nI was told to write the boxes off as spoiled. They were still warm when he took them, and I had eaten from the same batch.",anchor={scene="RBPizzaWhirled"}},
-- T0303
{id="t0303-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field dust on the wash pail",body="A hand shovel rests across a wash pail, both striped with yellow dust. The pail smells of crop spray; road tape is knotted through its handle.",anchor={scene="RBPoliceSiege"}},
{id="t0303-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Frequency held through the siege",body="The radio dial is bound with a narrow strip of tape. Its battery has been replaced recently, although the callers barricaded here had no way to send a reply. Someone wanted them listening to one channel.",anchor={scene="RBPoliceSiege"}},
-- T0304
{id="t0304-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Prayer list, Tuesday margin",body="In the margin I wrote that the orchard hands smelled of sweet spray and asked for water before service. Their youngest began shaking before the deputy closed the lane.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The notice changed faster than the deliveries, and no one came to collect what was left.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={scene="RBReverend"}},
{id="t0304-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A name left in the margin",body="I was asked to read the list aloud and I did. One name was missing, though the person was sitting right there. I thought the page had been copied badly.\n\nAfterward the visitor asked me not to add the name. She said another office had already settled it. The person stayed to help stack the chairs and asked why everyone had begun speaking softly.\n\nI wrote the name in the margin of my own book. It is not a record anyone will accept, but I could not bring myself to leave an empty space.",anchor={scene="RBReverend"}},
-- T0305
{id="t0305-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed dust under the bandages",body="A first-aid kit sits open beside a split seed sack. Yellow dust covers the gauze; black road tape is stuck to the sack.",anchor={scene="RBSWATStation"}},
{id="t0305-02",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A channel behind the lockers",body="The battery is new; the radio has been wrapped in a shirt to muffle it. A narrow strip of tape fixes the dial at the channel used before the order to leave.",anchor={scene="RBSWATStation"}},
-- T0306
{id="t0306-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The room nobody wanted",body="Thursday: the trial crew left their work shirts in the spare room. The sharp smell reached the kitchen, and the dog was sick before the road patrol arrived.\n\nThey counted the containers before anyone counted who had carried them. I wrote the second number here while I could still remember it.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={scene="RBSafehouse"}},
{id="t0306-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The extra occupant",body="They gave us a count for the beds and told us it was final. Then another family arrived at the back door with a child too tired to stand.\n\nWe made room and I put her shoes under the bed so nobody would trip. In the morning the list still had the old count. A visitor looked at the shoes and asked us to move them before the next inspection.\n\nThe child did not understand why her mother kept calling her by a different name. I did, but I did not tell her.",anchor={scene="RBSafehouse"}},
-- T0307
{id="t0307-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Two jars from the school garden",body="A cloudy water bottle and an empty sample jar share a strip of twine. Pale spray dust remains beneath both, inside the cupboard.",anchor={scene="RBSchool"}},
{id="t0307-02",kind="set",pieces={"Book","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Attendance from the wrong day",body="The roll book is open to an ordinary lesson. A pencil note on its back records a later head count, including pupils whose names are absent from the official list.",anchor={scene="RBSchool"}},
-- T0308
{id="t0308-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Soap bought after the field run",body="Soap, gloves, and two water jugs, paid cash. On the back: “Trial crew used the sink at dawn. My eyes burned before the road was shut.”\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={scene="RBShopLooted"}},
{id="t0308-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The inventory they took",body="The shelves were emptied twice. The first group took food; the second stepped over the broken glass to ask for the delivery ledger.\n\nI showed them the register because I had no ledger left. They wanted the names of people who had bought anything that morning. I could still recall one woman because her son carried the bag.\n\nThey wrote her down and told me not to mention their visit. I keep hearing the boy ask whether he could have the receipt.",anchor={scene="RBShopLooted"}},
-- T0309
{id="t0309-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The bucket with the bitter rinse",body="A mop has dried stiff across a bucket holding an oily film. The same film marks bootprints leading away from the kitchen shelf.",anchor={scene="RBSpiffo"}},
{id="t0309-02",kind="set",pieces={"DishCloth","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A clean counter and a missing roll",body="A fresh dish cloth lies under the register beside the empty spool where the morning receipts should be. Someone cleaned the counter after the rush, then removed only the record of it.",anchor={scene="RBSpiffo"}},
-- T0310
{id="t0310-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Photograph after the matinee",body="Written on the back: “The two men from the crop trial left yellow dust on every chair. We felt dizzy before the county van came.”\n\nThe person beside me recognized the handwriting and went quiet. We had been told not to rely on yesterday’s directions.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RBStripclub"}},
{id="t0310-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The last table",body="I wrote the closing time on the chalkboard. Later a man asked me to rub it out and say we had shut earlier.\n\nThe people at the last table were still here when he came in. One of them had gone to call a friend and left a coat behind. I did not know whether to give the coat back when the man took their names.\n\nThe board is clean. The coat is in the cupboard with my own things. If anyone comes for it, I will tell them when I last saw its owner.",anchor={scene="RBStripclub"}},
-- T0311
{id="t0311-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Breakfast beside an unopened kit",body="A wrapped loaf and first-aid kit are tied together with road tape. Fine field dust covers the bread bag, but the kit is clean.",anchor={scene="RBTSBreakfast"}},
{id="t0311-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The missing breakfast tally",body="Two bowls are stacked around a folded scrap with a count written on it. The number served is larger than the number entered in the book, though the food has already been eaten.",anchor={scene="RBTSBreakfast"}},
-- T0312
{id="t0312-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Freezer note in a butcher's hand",body="I wrote down the sour smell after the field truck unloaded its rinse barrels. The meat was still cold when the flies vanished and the siren began.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. When I asked, the person at the barrier looked at the seal instead and handed it back.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={scene="RBTSButcher"}},
{id="t0312-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A separate cut of meat",body="The shopkeeper made me bring the parcel through the back. He said the front counter was closed to anyone who had been beyond the roadblock.\n\nA visitor checked the wrapper but never asked what was inside. He took the slip with the customer name and left the parcel on the table. It began to drip while they argued about which list should keep the name.\n\nI washed the table when they left. The parcel was still there, and I could not decide whether throwing it away counted as a sale.",anchor={scene="RBTSButcher"}},
-- T0314
{id="t0314-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supper left with a soil jar",body="A potato cut in half sits beside a jar of gray field water. Both carry the same waxy residue along the rim.",anchor={scene="RBTSDinner"}},
{id="t0314-02",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Bowl"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A cleared place setting",body="A spoon is laid across a bowl with a penciled count on its underside. The number is two higher than the count entered beside the meal.",anchor={scene="RBTSDinner"}},
-- T0315
{id="t0315-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The drink I poured away",body="I saved the bottle for you because it smelled like the trial orchard after spraying. I poured out the glasses before the roadblock appeared.\n\nWe waited for a correction that never came. Every passing driver had a different instruction and no room for one more passenger.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={scene="RBTSDrink"}},
{id="t0315-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The drinks still owed",body="I put aside four glasses after the men came in. They said the others would be back for them and asked me to write the names on a napkin.\n\nI watched them pour the drinks away when they thought I had gone. The glasses were washed and returned to the shelf, but they kept the napkin.\n\nOne of the four had borrowed my coat. I still have the claim ticket for it, and no one will tell me where to take it.",anchor={scene="RBTSDrink"}},
-- T0316
{id="t0316-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Field radio with a fresh battery",body="A fresh battery is taped to a field radio. Green spray flecks fill the speaker grille, and the last tuning mark is below the county warning channel.",anchor={scene="RBTSElectronics"}},
{id="t0316-02",kind="set",pieces={"RadioBlack","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A receiver with a single mark",body="A radio sits beside a loose battery. A pencil mark on the dial matches one on the workbench; every other frequency has been scratched away.",anchor={scene="RBTSElectronics"}},
-- T0317
{id="t0317-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Recipe page, lower corner",body="My note says the farm crew washed their sample jars in this sink. The water turned milky; two hours later a patrol told us not to use the tap.\n\nNobody agreed on whose list this belonged to. I left it where the next person would look for the things we still owed each other.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={scene="RBTSFoodPreparation"}},
{id="t0317-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The missing cutting board",body="They told us to throw away the board but to leave the knife. I said we had served from both, and the man at the door asked only who had signed the delivery.\n\nMy helper had signed because I was late. She stayed behind to clean when they took the board. They asked for her address, then said she could go home.\n\nWe still have the order book. A page is gone, though the food from that order was already on the table.",anchor={scene="RBTSFoodPreparation"}},
-- T0318
{id="t0318-01",kind="set",pieces={"CannedCorn","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Lunch wrapped with a bandage",body="A can of corn and sealed bandage are wrapped in the same strip of road tape. Yellow field dust is trapped under the tape.",anchor={scene="RBTSSandwich"}},
{id="t0318-02",kind="set",pieces={"Spoon","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A sack beneath the sandwich tray",body="A spoon and a paperclip were caught in a folded feed sack used to line the tray. Its handwritten lot mark predates the closure notice pinned over it.",anchor={scene="RBTSSandwich"}},
-- T0319
{id="t0319-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hemmed cuffs from the trial field",body="Friday: I mended three work shirts from the seed trial. White powder shook from every cuff; my hands blistered before anyone closed the road.\n\nThe clerk wanted a cleaner version. I kept the stained one because it showed which part had been changed after the road closed.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={scene="RBTSSewing"}},
{id="t0319-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A sleeve sewn shut",body="The woman brought in a coat with its pocket torn. While I pinned it, a folded list fell out. She asked me to sew the pocket closed with the list inside.\n\nShe said her brother would need the coat if he returned. I offered to write his name on the label. She shook her head so hard she dropped the thread.\n\nI used a different color along the seam. If he comes back, someone can find the paper without ruining the whole coat.",anchor={scene="RBTSSewing"}},
-- T0320
{id="t0320-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","TinOpener"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cloudy water beside the soup",body="A cloudy water bottle stands beside a tin opener crusted with yellow dust. A hand-drawn line on the bottle marks the level before boiling.",anchor={scene="RBTSSoup"}},
{id="t0320-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bowl","Spoon"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The unserved bowl",body="One bowl is clean and tied to a second with string. The count scratched into the first was reduced in pencil on the other, though both were carried to the table.",anchor={scene="RBTSSoup"}},
-- T0321
{id="t0321-01",kind="set",pieces={"Saw","Plank"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A repair set aside",body="The tools match a small repair, but the spare was prepared before anyone recorded a fault.",anchor={scene="RBTrashed"}},
{id="t0321-02",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","HandShovel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The spoiled pail",body="A bucket bears a faded field lot mark beneath a newer cleaning label. A hand shovel still has the same fine yellow dust caught in its handle.",anchor={scene="RBTrashed"}},
-- T0322
{id="t0322-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Thursday after closing — a sweet chemical smell",body="I saved the cloth with a sweet chemical smell for you. The water-treatment trial crew passed Thursday after closing; the rats left the shed, and afterward the clinic stopped answering.\n\nI carried it home because there was nowhere open to return it. The mark did not come off when I tried to wash my hands.\n\nThe next morning I looked for a second copy and found only the envelope. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={scene="RBTwiggy"}},
{id="t0322-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The visitor at closing",body="A man sat by the back door and asked for the names of everyone who had come in. I assumed he meant the people still here.\n\nHe wanted the earlier customers too. I wrote down the one I knew because she brought her own mug. He crossed out her name, then asked whether I was certain she had arrived.\n\nHer mug is still under the counter. I have not washed it, though I cannot say what that proves.",anchor={scene="RBTwiggy"}},
-- T0323
{id="t0323-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and wash pail, friday before dawn",body="The hand shovel and wash pail share a bitter residue from the field-sprayer test. They were bundled before the radio warned everyone indoors.",anchor={scene="RBWoodcraft"}},
{id="t0323-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Carpenter’s margin",body="The men building shelves were told to make another partition before the evacuation trucks came. Someone measured for beds and then scratched the measurements out. My brother still brought his tools, because the invoice for the first day had already been paid.",anchor={scene="RBWoodcraft"}},
-- T0324
{id="t0324-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Saturday near lunch — a sharp solvent smell",body="Saturday near lunch: two workers from the crop plot carried a sharp solvent smell. two hens went still before the lane was closed.\n\nThe mark was made in a hurry, before the queue moved. I checked it twice against the people standing with me.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={scene="RDSBandPractice"}},
{id="t0324-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A rehearsal interrupted",body="We were halfway through the same song for the third time when a visitor came in and asked us to lower the volume. He needed to hear the radio in the hallway.\n\nThe voice on it was reading street names. One of us lived on the first street and went to call home. The visitor shut the door before the next name.\n\nWe tried to play again. Nobody could remember the first line, so I wrote the streets down instead.",anchor={scene="RDSBandPractice"}},
-- T0325
{id="t0325-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle, sunday after supper",body="The first-aid kit and water bottle are tied together. blue powder coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSBanditRaid"}},
{id="t0325-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A folded address beside the raid",body="A map and a pencil are kept together in a pocket. Three homes have been circled, but only one has been crossed off; the mark was made before the door was forced.",anchor={scene="RDSBanditRaid"}},
-- T0326
{id="t0326-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the night shift — white crystals",body="Personal note — the night shift: wash off the white crystals left by the livestock-feed study crew. the creek smelled wrong, and I had not yet heard that the siren began.\n\nI folded the corner so I could find the entry again. Someone wanted the book put away before I had even finished copying it.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={scene="RDSBathroomZed"}},
{id="t0326-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The names beyond the door",body="I heard someone knock while I was hiding here. He said he was checking the rooms and read a list aloud.\n\nThe name of the person with me was on it, though she had not told anyone we were here. She whispered that they had copied an older list from another building.\n\nHe left after we stayed quiet. I wrote the names I could remember so I can ask her later where that list came from.",anchor={scene="RDSBathroomZed"}},
-- T0327
{id="t0327-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cut potato and sample jar, the early shift",body="The cut potato and sample jar share red grit from the fertilizer test. They were bundled before the buses quit running.",anchor={scene="RDSBedroomZed"}},
{id="t0327-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bandage"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A label under the pillow",body="A bottle of water and a strip of bandage have matching pencil marks. The marks are dates, not doses; someone was checking this bed before its occupant woke.",anchor={scene="RDSBedroomZed"}},
-- T0328
{id="t0328-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the late afternoon — sticky pollen",body="I saved the cloth with sticky pollen for you. The orchard spray test crew passed the late afternoon; the mare refused her feed, and afterward the bridge was blocked.\n\nI had promised to bring this home for supper. Its date and the empty chair at the table now belong to the same evening.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={scene="RDSBleach"}},
{id="t0328-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The count in a coat pocket",body="I asked for clean water. The man with the bucket asked how many people were still here before he opened it.\n\nI pointed to the room behind me. He wrote down a smaller number and said the others would be counted separately. He would not say where.\n\nThe bucket was emptied on the floor after he left. I kept the scrap he dropped because it has the number he first wrote.",anchor={scene="RDSBleach"}},
-- T0329
{id="t0329-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and rinse bucket, the first hot day",body="The mop and rinse bucket share black specks from the pasture study. They were bundled before a patrol turned us back.",anchor={scene="RDSCorpsePsycho"}},
{id="t0329-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Sheet"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A folded list among the tools",body="A pencil and a torn sheet are folded together in a pocket. The sheet lists rooms by number, with the last two struck out in a different hand.",anchor={scene="RDSCorpsePsycho"}},
-- T0330
{id="t0330-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Monday morning — an oily film",body="Monday morning: two workers from the seed trial carried an oily film. my eyes began burning before the county van arrived.\n\nI meant to ask about it in the morning. By then the person who could answer had gone with the last vehicle, and this was all that remained.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={scene="RDSDeadDrunk"}},
{id="t0330-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="After the music stopped",body="We thought he had fallen asleep and left him on the couch. A man at the door asked us to write down when we had last spoken to him.\n\nHe wanted one time for all of us. We disagreed because some of us had left the room. He wrote down his own time and asked us to sign below it.\n\nI still have the bottle cap he put beside the paper to hold it flat. I do not know whose account that paper is supposed to be.",anchor={scene="RDSDeadDrunk"}},
-- T0331
{id="t0331-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and field radio, tuesday at dusk",body="The battery and field radio are tied together. green flecks coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSDevouredByRats"}},
{id="t0331-02",kind="set",pieces={"Paperclip","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count beneath the torn coat",body="The folded paper lists six arrivals and four departures. The pencil is tucked into the same pocket; two departures have been erased until the paper is almost transparent.",anchor={scene="RDSDevouredByRats"}},
-- T0332
{id="t0332-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wednesday before rain — gray foam",body="Personal note — Wednesday before rain: wash off the gray foam left by the feed additive trial crew. my brother started coughing, and I had not yet heard that a deputy taped off the road.\n\nI did not know where to put it after the shelves were cleared. There was still someone coming back for the answer written on it.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={scene="RDSFootballNight"}},
{id="t0332-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The score at halftime",body="At halftime we heard the street announcement through the open window. The others kept watching the game and I wrote the names of the roads on the back of the score sheet.\n\nSomeone came by after dark and asked me for it. He already knew the score and said he only wanted to check my spelling.\n\nI gave him the front half. The names are still here because I tore the page across the fold first.",anchor={scene="RDSFootballNight"}},
-- T0333
{id="t0333-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand axe and seed sack, thursday after closing",body="The hand axe and seed sack share milky water from the water-treatment trial. They were bundled before the clinic stopped answering.",anchor={scene="RDSGrouchos"}},
{id="t0333-02",kind="set",pieces={"DishCloth","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A cleaned pair of spectacles",body="A dish cloth is knotted around a water bottle. Inside it is a penciled count of people seen that afternoon, with one line altered after the cloth had been washed.",anchor={scene="RDSGrouchos"}},
-- T0334
{id="t0334-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Friday before dawn — yellow dust",body="I saved the cloth with yellow dust for you. The field-sprayer test crew passed Friday before dawn; three people felt dizzy, and afterward the radio warned everyone indoors.\n\nWe tried to finish the ordinary work around it. The notice changed faster than the deliveries, and no one came to collect what was left.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={scene="RDSGunmanInBathroom"}},
{id="t0334-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="What he said through the door",body="He told us to stay in the room and wait for the count. We could hear boots in the hall and someone asking whether to include the people behind the bathroom door.\n\nThe answer was no. They read out a number, then asked us to leave one at a time. He stayed behind with the door locked.\n\nI wrote the number down because it was smaller than the number of voices I had heard.",anchor={scene="RDSGunmanInBathroom"}},
-- T0335
{id="t0335-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wrapped loaf and canned corn, saturday near lunch",body="The wrapped loaf and canned corn share a sweet chemical smell from the crop plot. They were bundled before the lane was closed.",anchor={scene="RDSGunslinger"}},
{id="t0335-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A second route in the pocket",body="The map is folded open to a road that has been erased in pencil. A strip of tape on the back carries the earlier route, preserved after the printed one was changed.",anchor={scene="RDSGunslinger"}},
-- T0336
{id="t0336-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Sunday after supper — a bitter residue",body="Sunday after supper: two workers from the greenhouse trial carried a bitter residue. my hands blistered before the phones went dead.\n\nThey counted the containers before anyone counted who had carried them. I wrote the second number here while I could still remember it.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={scene="RDSHenDo"}},
{id="t0336-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The list for the party",body="We put the guests names on a sheet so we could keep the surprise. A stranger arrived with a copy that had two names removed.\n\nHe asked whether those two had already left. I said one was still upstairs, getting ready. He folded his copy and waited at the foot of the stairs.\n\nNobody wanted to spoil the party by arguing. I have kept our list because it is the only one with everyone on it.",anchor={scene="RDSHenDo"}},
-- T0337
{id="t0337-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and empty sprayer, the night shift",body="The fertilizer sack and empty sprayer are tied together. a sharp solvent smell coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSHockeyPsycho"}},
{id="t0337-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Paperclip"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A quiet inventory in a pocket",body="A notebook page is wrapped around a pencil. It counts three people at the door and four after it closed, with the extra tally squeezed into the margin.",anchor={scene="RDSHockeyPsycho"}},
-- T0338
{id="t0338-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the early shift — blue powder",body="Personal note — the early shift: wash off the blue powder left by the fertilizer test crew. the dog refused its water, and I had not yet heard that the buses quit running.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={scene="RDSHouseParty"}},
{id="t0338-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Someone took the guest book",body="We wrote names on the wall when the guest book disappeared. It was a joke until a visitor asked us to paint over them.\n\nOne friend had gone for more drinks and was not there to object. By morning somebody had covered only his name. The rest remained visible through the paint.\n\nI took a photograph before anyone did the second coat. I cannot tell if he came back while we were asleep.",anchor={scene="RDSHouseParty"}},
-- T0339
{id="t0339-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand shovel and wash pail, the late afternoon",body="The hand shovel and wash pail share white crystals from the orchard spray test. They were bundled before the bridge was blocked.",anchor={scene="RDSPokerNight"}},
{id="t0339-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Book"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="An empty seat at the table",body="A pencil lies through a ring of playing cards. The score sheet counts one more player than the chairs, and a later hand has rubbed the extra column thin.",anchor={scene="RDSPokerNight"}},
-- T0340
{id="t0340-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the first hot day — red grit",body="I saved the cloth with red grit for you. The pasture study crew passed the first hot day; the flies vanished, and afterward a patrol turned us back.\n\nThe person beside me recognized the handwriting and went quiet. We had been told not to rely on yesterday’s directions.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RDSPoliceAtHouse"}},
{id="t0340-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A number given at the door",body="They asked me to count the people inside while they were still walking through the house. I gave the number I knew.\n\nOne of them looked at a folded sheet and said it was too high. He asked whether a visitor had already gone home. The visitor was asleep upstairs.\n\nI left the number on the back of this envelope. If someone asks later, I want to remember what I actually saw.",anchor={scene="RDSPoliceAtHouse"}},
-- T0341
{id="t0341-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First-aid kit and water bottle, monday morning",body="The first-aid kit and water bottle share sticky pollen from the seed trial. They were bundled before the county van arrived.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscape"}},
{id="t0341-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="An exit marked twice",body="A pencil and map share the same pocket. One route is marked toward the road, then overwritten with a line back toward the building.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscape"}},
-- T0342
{id="t0342-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Tuesday at dusk — black specks",body="Tuesday at dusk: two workers from the pest-control test carried black specks. the garden browned before the checkpoint appeared.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. When I asked, the person at the barrier looked at the seal instead and handed it back.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscapeWithPolice"}},
{id="t0342-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The names at the gate",body="We reached the gate before dawn. A man with a list asked us to give our names one at a time.\n\nWhen my companion spoke, the man stopped writing and looked at the person beside him. They argued over which list to use. We could see the road was clear.\n\nThey let the others through. We were told to wait for a second count, and I wrote the first count here so it would not disappear.",anchor={scene="RDSPrisonEscapeWithPolice"}},
-- T0343
{id="t0343-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cut potato and sample jar, wednesday before rain",body="The cut potato and sample jar are tied together. an oily film coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSRPGNight"}},
{id="t0343-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Last game in the margin",body="We played until a man outside told us the road would be closed at dawn. He let the other car through and said the count had been made yesterday. I kept my score sheet; it is the only record that we were here.",anchor={scene="RDSRPGNight"}},
-- T0344
{id="t0344-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Thursday after closing — green flecks",body="Personal note — Thursday after closing: wash off the green flecks left by the water-treatment trial crew. the rats left the shed, and I had not yet heard that the clinic stopped answering.\n\nThe first account was spoken quickly, as if there might be a bus to catch. I wrote it down before another person could replace it.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={scene="RDSRatInfested"}},
{id="t0344-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="How many traps were set",body="I counted the traps because I thought that was why they came. The visitor asked instead which doors we had opened that morning.\n\nHe marked one room as empty before looking in it. When I asked him to check again, he said the number had already been sent.\n\nThe traps remain. The door he marked empty is shut now, and I do not want to be the person who opens it.",anchor={scene="RDSRatInfested"}},
-- T0345
{id="t0345-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Mop and rinse bucket, friday before dawn",body="The mop and rinse bucket share gray foam from the field-sprayer test. They were bundled before the radio warned everyone indoors.",anchor={scene="RDSRatWar"}},
{id="t0345-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A corrected tally by the wall",body="A water bottle is tied to a pencil with string. The scratched tally on the bottle differs from the number copied onto the sheet beside it.",anchor={scene="RDSRatWar"}},
-- T0346
{id="t0346-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Saturday near lunch — milky water",body="I saved the cloth with milky water for you. The crop plot crew passed Saturday near lunch; two hens went still, and afterward the lane was closed.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={scene="RDSResourceGarage"}},
{id="t0346-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The garage inventory",body="I told them which shelves had fuel and which held tools. They asked for the names of people who had filled containers the night before.\n\nI could remember the man who paid in coins because I had counted them twice. His number was already on their sheet. They did not ask me about the fuel after that.\n\nI put the coins away separately. The drawer still has the gap where the sheet had been kept.",anchor={scene="RDSResourceGarage"}},
-- T0347
{id="t0347-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery and field radio, sunday after supper",body="The battery and field radio share yellow dust from the greenhouse trial. They were bundled before the phones went dead.",anchor={scene="RDSSkeletonPsycho"}},
{id="t0347-02",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Rope"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A route folded into a pocket",body="The map is creased at the junction and tied with string. One destination has been erased so deeply that the paper nearly split; the route leading to it remains clear.",anchor={scene="RDSSkeletonPsycho"}},
-- T0348
{id="t0348-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the night shift — a sweet chemical smell",body="the night shift: two workers from the livestock-feed study carried a sweet chemical smell. the creek smelled wrong before the siren began.\n\nThere was a place for a signature and no one willing to write one. I used the margin to note what we actually found.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={scene="RDSSpecificProfession"}},
{id="t0348-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The wrong occupation",body="The man writing the names asked what I did for a living. I told him, and he put down something else.\n\nHe said the form had no space for my work. I could see there was a space; it was already filled. The person beside me told me to let him finish.\n\nI wrote my own occupation here because I do not want the next person to think I lied about it.",anchor={scene="RDSSpecificProfession"}},
-- T0349
{id="t0349-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Hand axe and seed sack, the early shift",body="The hand axe and seed sack are tied together. a bitter residue coats one side; a torn strip of road tape covers the other.",anchor={scene="RDSStagDo"}},
{id="t0349-02",kind="set",pieces={"GlassTumbler","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The extra name on the score",body="A sheet and pencil are tucked under an empty glass. The guest count was changed after the first toast, but the marks around the glass show it had been there all night.",anchor={scene="RDSStagDo"}},
-- T0350
{id="t0350-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="the late afternoon — a sharp solvent smell",body="Personal note — the late afternoon: wash off the a sharp solvent smell left by the orchard spray test crew. the mare refused her feed, and I had not yet heard that the bridge was blocked.\n\nI took the page when they shut the building. No one could tell me whether the missing line meant delayed, refused, or already gone.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={scene="RDSStudentNight"}},
{id="t0350-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A list after the lights went out",body="We were supposed to be studying. When the lights failed, we counted everyone by calling out names across the room.\n\nA visitor came with a shorter list and said two people had gone home. One of them answered from the far corner. He crossed her name out anyway.\n\nShe wanted to leave then, but none of us knew whether the door was still open. I kept this page with her name on it.",anchor={scene="RDSStudentNight"}},
-- T0351
{id="t0351-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wrapped loaf and canned corn, the first hot day",body="The wrapped loaf and canned corn share blue powder from the pasture study. They were bundled before a patrol turned us back.",anchor={scene="RDSSuicidePact"}},
{id="t0351-02",kind="set",pieces={"Sheet","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A third mark on the page",body="A folded sheet and pencil are held beneath the same hand. Two names are boxed together, while a third is pressed into the paper hard enough to leave a mark without ink.",anchor={scene="RDSSuicidePact"}},
-- T0352
{id="t0352-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Monday morning — white crystals",body="I saved the cloth with white crystals for you. The seed trial crew passed Monday morning; my eyes began burning, and afterward the county van arrived.\n\nI carried it home because there was nowhere open to return it. The mark did not come off when I tried to wash my hands.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={scene="RDSTinFoilHat"}},
{id="t0352-02",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The person at the window",body="I made a hat to keep the rain off the radio. It looked ridiculous, so nobody noticed when I carried it from room to room.\n\nThe same street names came through three times. After the second reading a visitor told us the broadcast had never happened and asked for the radio.\n\nI took the battery out first. The station may be silent now, but I want to know what it says if it comes back.",anchor={scene="RDSTinFoilHat"}},
-- T0353
{id="t0353-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer sack and empty sprayer, tuesday at dusk",body="The fertilizer sack and empty sprayer share red grit from the pest-control test. They were bundled before the checkpoint appeared.",anchor={scene="RDSZombieLockedBathroom"}},
{id="t0353-02",kind="set",pieces={"Pencil","Sheet"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count through a locked door",body="A pencil and sheet are pushed beneath the door together. The sheet has an earlier head count, then a later number written over it without any sign the door was opened.",anchor={scene="RDSZombieLockedBathroom"}},
-- T0355
{id="t0355-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Coat pocket note — after Monday supper",body="My coat pocket entry says the well-water study workers brushed off silver specks. the mice abandoned the bin before the nurse stopped taking calls.\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RDSZombiesEating"}},
{id="t0355-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Four names, three bodies",body="I counted four names in the book they carried, but only three people lay here. The man with the book asked me not to look for the fourth.\n\nHe turned the page toward me to show that the missing person had already been accounted for. The writing was too small to read and he closed it before I could ask.\n\nI wrote the four names as well as I remember them. I may have misspelled one, but I know I heard it.",anchor={scene="RDSZombiesEating"}},
-- T0356
{id="t0356-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Cut potato with a soil jar at at Tuesday dawn",body="The cut potato with a soil jar are tied in one bundle. a greasy sheen marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RVSAmbulanceCrash"}},
{id="t0356-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Harvest at the stretcher",body="My sister was brought from the treated rows before anybody called the ambulance. The crew asked for her work clothes to be put in a separate sack. By the time they reached us, three neighbors who never entered the field had the same burning eyes.",anchor={scene="RVSAmbulanceCrash"}},
-- T0357
{id="t0357-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cab note — late Wednesday",body="On the back: “late Wednesday, emerald flecks in the cab after the crop trial. the chickens stopped moving. Later, the back road closed.”\n\nI asked for the old page back after the new instructions arrived. They said it had been destroyed, but its corner was still in my pocket.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={scene="RVSAnimalTrailerOnRoad"}},
{id="t0357-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A crossing marked in pencil",body="The driver said the animals had to wait until the officials finished counting cars. He asked whether the trailer counted as one vehicle or several lives. They copied the plate and waved the empty truck ahead.",anchor={scene="RVSAnimalTrailerOnRoad"}},
-- T0358
{id="t0358-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Stiff mop with a rinse bucket at before Thursday lunch",body="The stiff mop with a rinse bucket carry brown foam from the greenhouse test. They were packed before the telephone line died.",anchor={scene="RVSBanditRoad"}},
{id="t0358-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Receipt for passage",body="The men at the road took our spare fuel and said the next checkpoint would let us through. I wrote the amount on the back of the grocery slip. There was no checkpoint there, only the cars they had already turned around.",anchor={scene="RVSBanditRoad"}},
-- T0359
{id="t0359-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Weathered bundle note — Friday at closing",body="Feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. My note below says chalky water came from the feed test; the ditch smelled metallic before the noon siren sounded.\n\nThe children asked why the same place had two different names on the two papers. I told them to hold on to both until we knew.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RVSBurntCar"}},
{id="t0359-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two copies of a plate",body="The car burned after they copied its registration onto the clear list. I watched them carry a new list to the far side of the road. My father was told he had never arrived, although his name was on my first copy.",anchor={scene="RVSBurntCar"}},
-- T0360
{id="t0360-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Battery with a field radio at Saturday before sunrise",body="The battery with a field radio carry mustard-colored dust from the fertilizer trial. They were packed before traffic was turned around.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrash"}},
{id="t0360-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A route after midnight",body="The driver had been told the south road was open to families. Someone moved the barrier while we stopped for water. He went back to ask and was offered a different map with the old road drawn out of it.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrash"}},
-- T0361
{id="t0361-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cab note — during the hot afternoon",body="My cab entry says the orchard treatment workers brushed off a cloying orchard smell. the horse kicked away its feed before the crossing was barricaded.\n\nMy mother put it with the household bills so it would not be thrown away. It was the only part of the week that still had a date.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashCorpse"}},
{id="t0361-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Passenger’s folded page",body="The person beside me waited in the car while I asked for help. A man in a vest said the crash happened outside the area they were collecting names from. I wrote ours down anyway, so somebody might look for both of us.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashCorpse"}},
-- T0362
{id="t0362-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Hand axe with a seed sack at on the cold night",body="The hand axe with a seed sack are tied in one bundle. an acrid film marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashDeer"}},
{id="t0362-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Grass along the shoulder",body="The deer came from a pasture that had been sprayed yesterday. Its mouth was wet with a bitter smell; the driver said the creek near the rows smelled the same. We had just crossed the county line and had not heard any warning about the fields.",anchor={scene="RVSCarCrashDeer"}},
-- T0363
{id="t0363-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Cab note — the first morning",body="On the back: “the first morning, a medicinal odor in the cab after the experimental seed run. my throat tightened. Later, county trucks reached us.”\n\nA pencil line had been rubbed thin but not erased. I could still read enough of it to recognize what had been there first.\n\nI do not know which of the two accounts was repeated afterward. The older one is the one I had in my hands that day.",anchor={scene="RVSChangingTire"}},
{id="t0363-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Tire chalk",body="A worker drew a chalk circle around the stopped car and promised a tow after the next convoy. The convoy arrived, took everyone able to walk, and crossed our names off his pad. I stayed to finish the tire and found the pad discarded.",anchor={scene="RVSChangingTire"}},
-- T0364
{id="t0364-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Wrapped bread with canned corn at the second evening",body="The wrapped bread with canned corn carry violet powder from the insecticide test. They were packed before a checkpoint opened.",anchor={scene="RVSConstructionSite"}},
{id="t0364-02",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","DuctTape","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Taped radio in the site truck",body="A work radio with its dial taped down on one channel, spare batteries beside it. Someone told the crew to stay off the air and listen only, days before the road was closed.",anchor={scene="RVSConstructionSite"}},
-- T0365
{id="t0365-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cab receipt before sunday's rain",body="feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. my note below says saltlike grains came from the livestock supplement test; my sister coughed all night before warning tape went up.\n\nWe kept one copy for ourselves. The person collecting the other one said the numbers would be corrected later, once everyone had moved.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={scene="RVSCrashHorde"}},
{id="t0365-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Last fuel stop",body="At the bend they made us wait for a lead car before letting anyone through. The lead car never returned. The man who kept the count quietly drew a line through everyone still waiting when the road filled up.",anchor={scene="RVSCrashHorde"}},
-- T0366
{id="t0366-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="fertilizer sack with a drained sprayer at after monday supper",body="the fertilizer sack with a drained sprayer carry rust-colored grit from the well-water study. they were packed before the nurse stopped taking calls.",anchor={scene="RVSDeadEnd"}},
{id="t0366-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The road ends twice",body="They painted an arrow to the exit, then shifted the barrier beyond the last turn. I walked back for my mother, who cannot climb the ditch. By then the painted arrow was covered and the man with the clipboard said he had seen no one.",anchor={scene="RVSDeadEnd"}},
-- T0367
{id="t0367-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cab note — at tuesday dawn",body="my cab entry says the sprayer trial workers brushed off waxy pollen. the driver grew dizzy before the shelter message aired.\n\nOur copy stayed on the kitchen table. The official account came later and asked us to remember a much shorter day.\n\nThe next morning I looked for a second copy and found only the envelope. I left this one unfolded for whoever came after us.",anchor={scene="RVSFlippedCrash"}},
{id="t0367-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The overturned list",body="A folded page inside the cab has the names of people assigned seats. Somebody crossed the whole column through and wrote “returned” above it. I saw the truck leave full. No one at the next road would say where its passengers had gone.",anchor={scene="RVSFlippedCrash"}},
-- T0368
{id="t0368-01",kind="set",pieces={"HandShovel","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="hand shovel with a scrub bucket at late wednesday",body="the hand shovel with a scrub bucket are tied in one bundle. silver specks marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockade"}},
{id="t0368-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed on the barricade",body="The patrol truck carried sacks from the farm test, with yellow dust on the seams. The officer said the cargo was being taken for safekeeping. A torn sack had already left a stripe across the road where people queued for water.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockade"}},
-- T0369
{id="t0369-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cab note — before thursday lunch",body="on the back: “before thursday lunch, a greasy sheen in the cab after the greenhouse test. my wrists blistered. later, the telephone line died.”\n\nThe person who handed this to me asked me to keep the date. I did, though the next version left that day out entirely.\n\nI wanted to keep a clean copy, but the stain is where the first entry was crossed out. I have not tried to improve it.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockadeShooting"}},
{id="t0369-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count after gunfire",body="I helped move the injured away from the barrier. Later an officer asked for the number of cars, not the number of people. He drew a fresh line under his total while two families were still behind the disabled van.",anchor={scene="RVSPoliceBlockadeShooting"}},
-- T0370
{id="t0370-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="first-aid kit with a water bottle at friday at closing",body="the first-aid kit with a water bottle carry emerald flecks from the feed test. they were packed before the noon siren sounded.",anchor={scene="RVSRegionalProfessionVehicle"}},
{id="t0370-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The empty roster",body="The service driver showed me a card saying she could cross because her trade was needed. At the barrier they let the van through but asked her helper to wait. She had no line for him on the roster, only a place for the tools.",anchor={scene="RVSRegionalProfessionVehicle"}},
-- T0371
{id="t0371-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cab note — saturday before sunrise",body="feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. my note below says brown foam came from the fertilizer trial; our cat hid from the water bowl before traffic was turned around.\n\nSomeone said the smell was only from cleaning. I kept the scrap because the same smell had followed us from the previous stop.\n\nWhen I returned, the window was closed and the board was blank. I kept the page because it was the only one with our address.",anchor={scene="RVSRichJerk"}},
{id="t0371-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The better car",body="He offered cash to get the road opened while the rest of us waited. The attendant counted the seats in his car and let him go. By morning our line had been listed as empty, though we had never moved.",anchor={scene="RVSRichJerk"}},
-- T0372
{id="t0372-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cut potato with a soil jar at during the hot afternoon",body="the cut potato with a soil jar carry chalky water from the orchard treatment. they were packed before the crossing was barricaded.",anchor={scene="RVSRoadKill"}},
{id="t0372-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Counting the shoulder",body="The highway worker kept a tally of cars that stopped beside the dead animal. He was ordered to leave out the cars that turned around before reaching the barrier. My uncle was in one of those cars; we found his blanket by the milepost.",anchor={scene="RVSRoadKill"}},
-- T0373
{id="t0373-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cab note — on the cold night",body="my cab entry says the pasture treatment workers brushed off mustard-colored dust. not one fly remained before a cruiser waved us away.\n\nThe small ordinary expense was the part I could still account for. I could not make the other figure on this page match what I had seen.\n\nI could have mistaken the order in which those things happened. I could not mistake the empty place left for the person we had been waiting for.",anchor={scene="RVSTrailerCrash"}},
{id="t0373-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Trailer manifest",body="I watched them seal the trailer, then ask the driver to take the family home by a route that had already closed. He asked for the children to be counted with the cargo because the passenger column was full. Nobody laughed.",anchor={scene="RVSTrailerCrash"}},
-- T0374
{id="t0374-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="stiff mop with a rinse bucket at the first morning",body="the stiff mop with a rinse bucket are tied in one bundle. a cloying orchard smell marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RVSUtilityVehicle"}},
{id="t0374-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The roadside sprayer",body="A maintenance crew carried a tank used on the trial rows, still damp around the valve. They were sent to wash the road before the line of vehicles passed. I saw a worker rinse his hands in a ditch that flowed toward the houses.",anchor={scene="RVSUtilityVehicle"}},
-- T0375
{id="t0375-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — the second evening",body="on the back: “the second evening, an acrid film in the weathered bundle after the insecticide test. the tomato plants curled. later, a checkpoint opened.”\n\nWe waited for a correction that never came. Every passing driver had a different instruction and no room for one more passenger.\n\nPerhaps the new instructions were meant to help us. They arrived after we had already followed the old ones.",anchor={scene="RZSBBQParty"}},
{id="t0375-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Ash from the picnic",body="The party stayed after the announced closing time because the official road out was marked open on the paper. When the cars got there, a worker said the paper was from yesterday. We used it to start the fire when the night turned cold.",anchor={scene="RZSBBQParty"}},
-- T0376
{id="t0376-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="battery with a field radio at before sunday's rain",body="the battery with a field radio carry a medicinal odor from the livestock supplement test. they were packed before warning tape went up.",anchor={scene="RZSBaseball"}},
{id="t0376-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Scoreboard of arrivals",body="They promised a ride for everyone still at the field after the game. The volunteer wrote down jerseys instead of names and told two siblings in ordinary clothes to wait. The bus left with empty seats and the list said full.",anchor={scene="RZSBaseball"}},
-- T0377
{id="t0377-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — after monday supper",body="feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. my note below says violet powder came from the well-water study; the mice abandoned the bin before the nurse stopped taking calls.\n\nNobody agreed on whose list this belonged to. I left it where the next person would look for the things we still owed each other.\n\nI thought someone would ask for this at the gate. They asked instead how many were in the car, and let the paper stay in my hand.",anchor={scene="RZSBeachParty"}},
{id="t0377-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The last shore road",body="A handwritten note beside the coolers says the coastal road was open through sundown. Someone came back for a forgotten shoe after dark and found the gate shut. The person responsible for the sign had gone home with the only key.",anchor={scene="RZSBeachParty"}},
-- T0378
{id="t0378-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="hand axe with a seed sack at at tuesday dawn",body="the hand axe with a seed sack carry saltlike grains from the sprayer trial. they were packed before the shelter message aired.",anchor={scene="RZSBurntWreck"}},
{id="t0378-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The wrecked permit",body="The car had a windshield pass for a route officially clear of traffic. At the next crossing the guards had a revised list and would not honor it. The driver folded the pass into quarters to keep it dry for his wife.",anchor={scene="RZSBurntWreck"}},
-- T0379
{id="t0379-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — late wednesday",body="my weathered bundle entry says the crop trial workers brushed off rust-colored grit. the chickens stopped moving before the back road closed.\n\nThe clerk wanted a cleaner version. I kept the stained one because it showed which part had been changed after the road closed.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={scene="RZSBuryingCamp"}},
{id="t0379-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Names beneath the soil",body="I wrote down who we buried because the visitors collecting the numbers had counted tents instead of people. They asked for the notebook and left me the page for supplies. I kept this page folded under the coffee tin.",anchor={scene="RZSBuryingCamp"}},
-- T0380
{id="t0380-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="wrapped bread with canned corn at before thursday lunch",body="the wrapped bread with canned corn are tied in one bundle. waxy pollen marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RZSCampsite"}},
{id="t0380-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bitter rain at camp",body="We pitched the tent beyond the trial orchard because they said the fields were the only treated ground. Rain ran down the canvas and left the same yellow dust on our cups. My daughter had not eaten anything from the orchard.",anchor={scene="RZSCampsite"}},
-- T0381
{id="t0381-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — friday at closing",body="on the back: “friday at closing, silver specks in the weathered bundle after the feed test. the ditch smelled metallic. later, the noon siren sounded.”\n\nThe first person who saw it called it routine. The second asked me to stop using the well until another visit could be arranged.\n\nThe amount mattered to the office more than the people waiting outside. We stayed until dark because the last line still said to wait.",anchor={scene="RZSCharcoalBurner"}},
{id="t0381-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Burning the old directions",body="The ranger had given us a route out and said to keep the slip clean. A second ranger came before dark and told us the route had never been assigned. We used the old slip for tinder, except this corner with my mother’s name.",anchor={scene="RZSCharcoalBurner"}},
-- T0382
{id="t0382-01",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="fertilizer sack with a drained sprayer at saturday before sunrise",body="the fertilizer sack with a drained sprayer carry a greasy sheen from the fertilizer trial. they were packed before traffic was turned around.",anchor={scene="RZSDean"}},
{id="t0382-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A head count by the fire",body="Our camp was told the pickup would stop where the smoke could be seen. A vehicle came, copied the number of tents, and drove away before the sleeping people woke. The next day someone had crossed our site off the rescue map.",anchor={scene="RZSDean"}},
-- T0383
{id="t0383-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — during the hot afternoon",body="feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. my note below says emerald flecks came from the orchard treatment; the horse kicked away its feed before the crossing was barricaded.\n\nI set it aside to show the neighbor when she returned. Her porch was empty by the time the light was good enough to read it.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={scene="RZSFishingTrip"}},
{id="t0383-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The bank after closing",body="The fishing party was told to wait for a boat after the bridge closed. A patrol crossed upstream with room aboard, but its passenger sheet was filled out already. We waved a tackle box until our arms hurt.",anchor={scene="RZSFishingTrip"}},
-- T0384
{id="t0384-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="hand shovel with a scrub bucket at on the cold night",body="the hand shovel with a scrub bucket carry brown foam from the pasture treatment. they were packed before a cruiser waved us away.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCamp"}},
{id="t0384-02",kind="set",pieces={"RadioReceiver","Map","Pills"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Receiver and map left at the cold camp",body="A small receiver still set to an emergency band, a folded road map with the county roads crossed out in the same neat hand, and a strip of pills. The campers left before anyone announced a closure.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCamp"}},
-- T0385
{id="t0385-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — the first morning",body="my weathered bundle entry says the experimental seed run workers brushed off chalky water. my throat tightened before county trucks reached us.\n\nNo one wanted to keep the wet copy. It dried unevenly, and the ink from the first entry stayed visible beneath the second.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCampEaten"}},
{id="t0385-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Under the bedroll",body="I was told everyone here had been collected in the morning. I still heard my neighbor calling from the other tent when the men packed up their list. I wrote her name where their pencil had left a blank.",anchor={scene="RZSForestCampEaten"}},
-- T0386
{id="t0386-01",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="first-aid kit with a water bottle at the second evening",body="the first-aid kit with a water bottle are tied in one bundle. mustard-colored dust marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RZSHermitCamp"}},
{id="t0386-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Seed dust in the shelter",body="The old man had no part in the farm trial, yet a yellow rim formed around his water pail after the storm. He kept the first pail for washing and gave guests the second. The stream comes down from the same treated slope.",anchor={scene="RZSHermitCamp"}},
-- T0387
{id="t0387-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — before sunday's rain",body="on the back: “before sunday's rain, a cloying orchard smell in the weathered bundle after the livestock supplement test. my sister coughed all night. later, warning tape went up.”\n\nI asked for the old page back after the new instructions arrived. They said it had been destroyed, but its corner was still in my pocket.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RZSHillbillyHoedown"}},
{id="t0387-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The dance list",body="We counted people for a ride home by the pairs on the dance card. The driver was instructed to use the official total, two fewer than ours. He asked the two without partners to stand by the road until another truck came.",anchor={scene="RZSHillbillyHoedown"}},
-- T0388
{id="t0388-01",kind="set",pieces={"Potato","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cut potato with a soil jar at after monday supper",body="the cut potato with a soil jar carry an acrid film from the well-water study. they were packed before the nurse stopped taking calls.",anchor={scene="RZSHunterCamp"}},
{id="t0388-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Hunter’s return",body="The group came back to find a notice saying the camp had been cleared. Their boots were still here and the fire was warm. I carried the notice along the trail because I knew the youngest had gone for water.",anchor={scene="RZSHunterCamp"}},
-- T0389
{id="t0389-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="coat pocket note — at tuesday dawn",body="feed, soap, and a clean jar, paid cash. my note below says a medicinal odor came from the sprayer trial; the driver grew dizzy before the shelter message aired.\n\nThe children asked why the same place had two different names on the two papers. I told them to hold on to both until we knew.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={scene="RZSMurderScene"}},
{id="t0389-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="corpse",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Pocket list of witnesses",body="I heard three shots, then the person taking statements told me the file would say two. He said the third sound might have come from a car door. I put a mark beside it, because the woman on the ground heard it too.",anchor={scene="RZSMurderScene"}},
-- T0390
{id="t0390-01",kind="set",pieces={"Mop","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="stiff mop with a rinse bucket at late wednesday",body="the stiff mop with a rinse bucket carry violet powder from the crop trial. they were packed before the back road closed.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFest"}},
{id="t0390-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Attendance at the stage",body="The festival volunteers were asked to count exits while the music still played. The man at the gate kept the old total when the rear fence came down. He said correcting it would delay the buses.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFest"}},
-- T0391
{id="t0391-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — before thursday lunch",body="my weathered bundle entry says the greenhouse test workers brushed off saltlike grains. my wrists blistered before the telephone line died.\n\nMy mother put it with the household bills so it would not be thrown away. It was the only part of the week that still had a date.\n\nSomeone had to finish the household list even though the office had closed. I wrote the names in the space left for expenses.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFestStage"}},
{id="t0391-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A second set list",body="The singer stopped to tell the crowd where the exit was. A marshal took the microphone and pointed in the other direction, toward the closed service lane. The next morning the printed directions still showed the first exit.",anchor={scene="RZSMusicFestStage"}},
-- T0392
{id="t0392-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="battery with a field radio at friday at closing",body="the battery with a field radio are tied in one bundle. rust-colored grit marks the field side; torn warning tape marks the other.",anchor={scene="RZSNastyMattress"}},
{id="t0392-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A mattress by the ditch",body="The woman had been sleeping beside a field where the trial sprayers passed at dawn. She moved her bedding when the smell reached it, but the pale film returned overnight. Nobody in camp had seen a warning sign.",anchor={scene="RZSNastyMattress"}},
-- T0393
{id="t0393-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="weathered bundle note — saturday before sunrise",body="on the back: “saturday before sunrise, waxy pollen in the weathered bundle after the fertilizer trial. our cat hid from the water bowl. later, traffic was turned around.”\n\nA pencil line had been rubbed thin but not erased. I could still read enough of it to recognize what had been there first.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={scene="RZSOccultActivity"}},
{id="t0393-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Names after the candles",body="They gathered here after the road was closed, and someone carefully counted every person present. The official tally for this stretch was zero. The woman with the candles made a second list on the back of a wrapper.",anchor={scene="RZSOccultActivity"}},
-- T0394
{id="t0394-01",kind="set",pieces={"Axe","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="hand axe with a seed sack at during the hot afternoon",body="the hand axe with a seed sack carry silver specks from the orchard treatment. they were packed before the crossing was barricaded.",anchor={scene="RZSOldFirepit"}},
{id="t0394-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Firepit directions",body="The group burned the map after the marked road failed them. One corner survived with an arrow pointing to a station that had stopped taking arrivals. I recognized my own handwriting on the corner; I had copied the directions from a uniformed man.",anchor={scene="RZSOldFirepit"}},
-- T0396
{id="t0396-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="rain under the shelter roof",body="Tuesday: the pasture-test workers slept here with gray foam on their boots. The creek tasted bitter before warning tape appeared across the trail.\n\nThey counted the containers before anyone counted who had carried them. I wrote the second number here while I could still remember it.\n\nThere may be a simple reason for the change. Nobody at the next stop could tell us what to do with the first version.",anchor={scene="RZSOldShelter"}},
{id="t0396-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Inside the dry seam",body="We stayed under this roof because the trail below was listed as an evacuation route. A runner came back saying the gate at its end had been chained before noon. I left a dry blanket here for whoever believed the same sign.",anchor={scene="RZSOldShelter"}},
-- T0397
{id="t0397-01",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","EmptyJar"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="cloudy water beside a sample jar",body="A cloudy bottle and sample jar share a waxy green film. A scrap of twine around both still holds treated pasture grass.",anchor={scene="RZSOrphanedFawn"}},
{id="t0397-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The fawn tally",body="The ranger brought the fawn to the road and asked for a wildlife pickup. The checkpoint worker recorded one animal and no people, though the child holding its blanket stood beside him. She was still there when they shut the lane.",anchor={scene="RZSOrphanedFawn"}},
-- T0398
{id="t0398-01",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="torn note from the north trail",body="Personal note: the insecticide crew crossed at dawn, leaving yellow dust on the grass. The deer fled before the county trucks reached the trail.\n\nI saved it from the bag of rubbish because there was a name on the reverse. The name was not on the list they posted.\n\nIt could be a mistake in the copying. The things stacked beside the page were real enough, and still waiting to be moved.",anchor={scene="RZSRangerSmith"}},
{id="t0398-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A patrol in pencil",body="The north trail was marked clear after the patrol turned back halfway. I asked why my brother’s campsite appeared on the completed section. The ranger said the box only had room for one kind of mark.",anchor={scene="RZSRangerSmith"}},
-- T0399
{id="t0399-01",kind="set",pieces={"Battery","RadioBlack"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="field radio wrapped in warning tape",body="A fresh battery and field radio are wrapped together. Red field grit fills the speaker; county warning tape covers the tuning dial.",anchor={scene="RZSRockerParty"}},
{id="t0399-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Between two songs",body="A road crew passed the gathering and said there would be transport at daylight. The handwritten passenger list filled before the first vehicle arrived. The musicians kept playing so the people at the far end would not hear the argument.",anchor={scene="RZSRockerParty"}},
-- T0400
{id="t0400-01",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="letter folded beneath the bedroll",body="I kept the gloves with blue powder from the seed trial. Our dog stopped drinking before the road patrol turned us back toward camp.\n\nThe person beside me recognized the handwriting and went quiet. We had been told not to rely on yesterday’s directions.\n\nThe person who was supposed to collect it had no time to stop. I did not put it back with the rest of the ordinary papers.",anchor={scene="RZSSadCamp"}},
{id="t0400-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Shelter allocation",body="The camp had four spaces marked on the board but five people sleeping under the canvas. The volunteer tried to add one line after the supply truck departed. Someone had already sent the board’s total onward.",anchor={scene="RZSSadCamp"}},
-- T0401
{id="t0401-01",kind="set",pieces={"Garbagebag","Gloves_LeatherGloves"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="work gloves tied inside a trash sack",body="Leather gloves sit inside a knotted trash sack. Mustard-colored crop dust coats the cuffs, while the outside remains clean.",anchor={scene="RZSSexyTime"}},
{id="t0401-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The folded coat label",body="They left in a hurry when a patrol announced this area was clear. One of them went back for a coat, and the patrol told her no one had been here since morning. The date on the coat label was today.",anchor={scene="RZSSexyTime"}},
-- T0402
{id="t0402-01",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="camp notebook, page torn short",body="My entry says the orchard crew rinsed its sprayer upstream. The water turned milky, and my hands blistered before the bridge was blocked.\n\nI thought the date would settle it. When I asked, the person at the barrier looked at the seal instead and handed it back.\n\nI wrote the time before I went back for the others. The clock may have been slow; the second vehicle was already gone.",anchor={scene="RZSSurvivalistCamp"}},
{id="t0402-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Supplies for the wrong route",body="The survivalist had packed for a three-day hike along the official safe corridor. At its first crossing a new barrier sent him back toward the town he had left. He wrote the change in the margin so he would not trust the printed route again.",anchor={scene="RZSSurvivalistCamp"}},
-- T0403
{id="t0403-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","CannedCorn"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="picnic food under pale field dust",body="A wrapped loaf and can of corn carry the same pale field dust. The loaf is tied shut with twine cut from a treated seed sack.",anchor={scene="RZSTragicPicnic"}},
{id="t0403-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A family count on a napkin",body="At the picnic we were told a vehicle would come for each household. The first driver counted blankets spread on the grass instead. My little niece carried none, so I wrote her name twice to make sure she was seen.",anchor={scene="RZSTragicPicnic"}},
-- T0404
{id="t0404-01",kind="written",pieces={"photograph"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="photograph of an empty trap line",body="On the back: “No animals after the pasture trial sprayed. The sharp smell reached camp before the noon siren.”\n\nThe first account was spoken quickly, as if there might be a bus to catch. I wrote it down before another person could replace it.\n\nThe younger one wanted to throw it away. I promised we would ask in the morning, and put it where neither of us could forget.",anchor={scene="RZSTrapperCamp"}},
{id="t0404-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Trap line closure",body="The trapper was asked to clear the path for evacuation and left his traps open as instructed. The promised vehicles never used it. He went back at dusk to close the traps so no one walking in the dark would be hurt.",anchor={scene="RZSTrapperCamp"}},
-- T0405
{id="t0405-01",kind="set",pieces={"KeyRing","FirstAidKit"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="van keys tied to a first-aid kit",body="The van keys and first-aid kit share one cord. Green field flecks mark the keys; a strip of road tape seals the kit.",anchor={scene="RZSVanCamp"}},
{id="t0405-02",kind="set",pieces={"Rope","Gloves_LeatherGloves","MeasuringTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="vehicle",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Rope and gloves from a roadside perimeter",body="A coil of rope cut into equal lengths, work gloves, and a measuring tape stopped at the same mark each time. Somebody was measuring out a perimeter around the vans, not a camp.",anchor={scene="RZSVanCamp"}},
-- T0406
{id="t0406-01",kind="written",pieces={"receipt"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="feed-store receipt under the drums",body="Soap, work gloves, and two sample jars, paid cash. My note says the fertilizer crew left oily residue here before the road was closed.\n\nWe needed the supplies listed here for the following morning. The people who took the count left without asking whether we had them.\n\nIt may have started elsewhere; none of us saw the beginning. I only know what had reached this place before they closed the road.",anchor={scene="RZSWasteDump"}},
{id="t0406-02",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The disposal count",body="The hauler was told the dump road was clear and took a detour to avoid the crowded main route. The gate had been welded shut that morning. He wrote down the time because the dispatch sheet still charged him for arriving late.",anchor={scene="RZSWasteDump"}},
-- T0407
{id="t0407-01",kind="set",pieces={"Bucket","WaterBottle"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="bitter water saved beside the pump",body="A bucket and capped water bottle hold the same gray foam. Yellow spray dust circles both rims, above the waterline.",anchor={scene="RZSWaterPump"}},
{id="t0407-02",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="ground",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A queue for water",body="They shut the pump after assigning the households one pail apiece. More people came from the road, but their names belonged to a different district on the list. My father shared his pail while the clerk went to find another page.",anchor={scene="RZSWaterPump"}},
-- T0408
{id="t0408-01",kind="set",pieces={"Map","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The count beneath the route at first light",body="A road is rubbed out on the map, while six small figures remain beside it. The pencil has worn through the paper at the place where they waited. The date is on the wrapper, not on the object."},
{id="t0408-02",kind="set",pieces={"Clipboard","Eraser"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A tally without passengers at first light",body="The board lists four vehicle numbers and no names. An erased fifth line still bears the pressure of a child’s small handwriting. A strip of cloth keeps the pair together."},
{id="t0408-03",kind="set",pieces={"FirstAidKit","BathTowel"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Supplies for an empty seat at first light",body="The sealed kit is tied to a towel marked for a passenger. The seat allocation has been crossed off, though the towel is still damp. The corner still bears a hurried thumbprint."},
{id="t0408-04",kind="set",pieces={"Map","SheetPaper2"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two directions in one fold at first light",body="The loose page gives a route at odds with the one inked on the map. Someone has traced both with a finger stained from a lunch wrapper. One edge was kept dry beneath a coat."},
{id="t0408-05",kind="set",pieces={"HandTorch","Battery"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The lamp after closing at first light",body="The battery is taped to a torch beside a handwritten departure time. Its owner waited long enough to use up the spare. A short tally was added after the bundle was tied."},
{id="t0408-06",kind="set",pieces={"Badge","RubberBand"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="An unissued place in line at first light",body="A badge and a band for counting arrivals are tied together. The band has an extra notch that never made it onto the badge. The string has been retied since morning."},
{id="t0408-07",kind="set",pieces={"Jack","LugWrench"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Repair before the barrier at first light",body="The jack bears fresh road grit and the wrench a strip of warning tape. The repair was abandoned beside a penciled clearance time. The date is on the wrapper, not on the object."},
{id="t0408-08",kind="set",pieces={"WalkieTalkie1","Pencil"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The second signal at first light",body="A frequency is scratched into the pencil’s paint. The radio’s own label names another channel, and the paper wrapped around it says to wait. A strip of cloth keeps the pair together."},
{id="t0408-09",kind="set",pieces={"Notebook","RedPen"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="One more household at first light",body="A penciled household count ends at six. A red pen adds one name in the margin and then runs out before the line for a seat. The corner still bears a hurried thumbprint."},
{id="t0408-10",kind="set",pieces={"Bag_Schoolbag","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Packed for the wrong stop at first light",body="The bag contains an unused lunch wrapper; the map is folded to a stop crossed out twice. A child wrote the original time on the strap. One edge was kept dry beneath a coat."},
-- T0409
{id="t0409-01",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","SeedBag"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A jar beyond the rows at first light",body="The jar is dusted with the same yellow grains as the torn sack. Its label names a test plot, but the string tying them together is wet with roadside mud. The date is on the wrapper, not on the object."},
{id="t0409-02",kind="set",pieces={"WaterBottle","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Water kept for comparison at first light",body="A clean bottle and a cloudy bucket share a chalk mark. The bucket was filled far from the rows after the sprayer passed. A strip of cloth keeps the pair together."},
{id="t0409-03",kind="set",pieces={"Gloves_LeatherGloves","GardeningSprayEmpty"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The gloves used twice at first light",body="One cuff holds field dust; the other is stained with kitchen soap. The empty sprayer was carried past a household door. The corner still bears a hurried thumbprint."},
{id="t0409-04",kind="set",pieces={"AnimalFeedBag","Bucket"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Feed beside a rinse pail at first light",body="The feed sack has an oily streak beneath its fold. A rinse pail carries the same mark above the waterline. One edge was kept dry beneath a coat."},
{id="t0409-05",kind="set",pieces={"SeedBag","DuctTape"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The unopened seed allotment at first light",body="Tape seals a slit in the seed sack, but the pale dust beneath it is caught on the outside. A child’s height is marked on the tape. A short tally was added after the bundle was tied."},
{id="t0409-06",kind="set",pieces={"EmptyJar","Map"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A sample without its field at first light",body="The jar’s paper label names a trial row. A thumbprint in its residue falls on a different roadside mark on the map. The string has been retied since morning."},
{id="t0409-07",kind="set",pieces={"Bread","DishCloth"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Bread under field dust at first light",body="The loaf was wrapped in a clean cloth. Yellow powder lies between the cloth and the crust, though the knot was never opened. The date is on the wrapper, not on the object."},
{id="t0409-08",kind="set",pieces={"Soap2","Sponge"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The wash that failed at first light",body="The sponge is green at the center and the soap is worn only on one edge. Both were wrapped in a bag beside a small cup. A strip of cloth keeps the pair together."},
{id="t0409-09",kind="set",pieces={"GardeningSprayEmpty","Postcard"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A warning carried home at first light",body="The card asks for supper to be kept warm. A ring from the sprayer crosses the writing before the ink has dried. The corner still bears a hurried thumbprint."},
{id="t0409-10",kind="set",pieces={"Fertilizer","GlassTumbler"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Fertilizer and a dry cup at first light",body="Fine grains cling to the rim of a drinking glass. The fertilizer sack beside it was sealed with household thread. One edge was kept dry beneath a coat."},
