{id="t0425-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="First rain on the roof — in the margin",body="The first rain after the field treatment left yellow flecks in a pan under the leak. We had shut the window before the truck came. I saved the pan because no one believed me when I described it.\n\nThe dog would no longer drink from the dish left outside. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0425-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A receipt from the seed counter — in the margin",body="The receipt includes a small charge for sample jars. The shopkeeper wrote a household address beside it, not a field number. I asked why, and he said the delivery men used whatever route remained open.\n\nThe shop had already closed before I could return with the question. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
-- T0426
{id="t0426-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The route on the kitchen copy — after the rain",body="They told us the road was still open. The map pinned beside the shopping list had already been changed in pencil, and the neighbor who came for water said the gate was locked.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0426-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A place under the names — after the rain",body="I counted everyone in the queue before I counted cars. The person carrying the list wrote down the cars first and ran out of room for the family walking behind them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0426-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The second pickup time — after the rain",body="My brother stayed for the later vehicle because our aunt could not get into the first. Its time was written on the back of a lunch receipt. No driver at the next barrier knew of it.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0426-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Inside the crossed square — after the rain",body="The house was marked cleared while we were still packing. I put a square around the date on our own copy. We waited for someone to return and ask who was inside.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0426-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A seat counted twice — after the rain",body="The woman at the gate read our names aloud and put us on a bus list. Another person came out with a new list and said the first bus had already taken us.\n\nI left room for a correction and carried the paper through the night. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0426-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The return line — after the rain",body="A man in a vest promised to come back after he moved the first group. His pencil left an unfinished arrow on my paper. I kept the page when the rest of the notices were pulled down.\n\nThe last vehicle passed with space for the supplies but none listed for us. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0426-07",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="After the barrier moved — after the rain",body="We followed the directions given at dawn and found a chain across the road. Someone had moved the crossing but left the old sign standing. My father had memorized its distance because he could not read the smaller print.\n\nI kept the older copy in a coat pocket while everyone else was told to use the new one. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0426-08",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="A count made indoors — after the rain",body="The clerk counted the beds as if each held one person. My mother was sitting beside my sister, waiting for her to stand. On the posted total there was only one of them.\n\nThe youngest still asked whether the driver knew where we were. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0426-09",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="The parcel that returned — after the rain",body="I sent a change of address with the driver who said he could cross. The parcel came back with the new address rubbed out. The note from my husband inside had never been opened.\n\nThe pencil count did not change when the people standing beside me did. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0426-10",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="containment",rival="agricultural"}},title="Two versions of the line — after the rain",body="I copied the first line because it included our street. The replacement left the street out but retained the same number of vehicles. We stood beside the mailbox until the engines were gone.\n\nThe person who had written the first directions could no longer be found. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
-- T0427
{id="t0427-01",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A mark above the water — after the rain",body="The bottle looked clean until it dried, when a green line appeared above the water. We had filled it after the field truck passed, at a tap on the other side of the road.\n\nThe dog would no longer drink from the dish left outside. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0427-02",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The garden after misting — after the rain",body="I covered the herbs when the trial vehicle passed. By evening the leaves under the cover had curled too. The neighbor said the spray could not have crossed the fence, but her laundry had the same pale grains.\n\nThe shop had already closed before I could return with the question. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
{id="t0427-03",kind="written",pieces={"letter"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Supper from the wrong side — after the rain",body="The feed-store driver left a sack and stopped to wash his hands before accepting a cup of tea. He asked us not to use the rain barrel. His warning never appeared on the delivery slip.\n\nThe next family along the road noticed the smell without seeing the truck. We compared what we had seen with what was written there. The second account omitted the small part that had frightened us."},
{id="t0427-04",kind="written",pieces={"notepad"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="Boots by the threshold — after the rain",body="The workers removed their boots outside. By morning the pale dust had traveled inside on the dog’s paws. No one in the house had gone near the trial rows.\n\nI wrote down the day because the first warning arrived after it. I left the date on the page and did not try to straighten the damaged edge. Someone else might remember the same afternoon."},
{id="t0427-05",kind="written",pieces={"diary"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="The jar in a grocery bag — after the rain",body="I was asked to keep this sample apart from the cooking jars. Its lid came loose on the way back from the orchard. The grocery bag was set on the table before I noticed the smell.\n\nThe child’s blanket was drying nearby and held the same fine dust. My family asked me to put the paper away with the bills. I kept it separate because the person involved might come back for it."},
{id="t0427-06",kind="written",pieces={"notebook"},where={{place="mapNamed",spot="furniture",lean="agricultural",rival="containment"}},title="A fence too late — after the rain",body="They painted the boundary posts after the field test was done. The path we use for water lies beyond the last post. We had walked it that morning with the children.\n\nWe washed the small cup twice and put it away from the others. I had meant to save it only until someone could explain the difference. By then the ordinary work around us had stopped."},
